{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf","id":830298,"title":"Interview with new White Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-15T10:23:10-08:00","id":830298,"title":"Interview with new White Wolf","content":"imagonem.org/2016/02/15/white-wolfs-lead-storyteller-there-will-be-a-release-in-2016/<br /> <br /> I really, really don't like the look of things here; the overly edgy tone, the statement that roleplaying games don't sell and that they'll focus almost entirely on videogames, the insistence that pushing the envelope and doing things like working 9/11 into the fluff are good... this just smacks of a shallow corporate buyout by people who don't have a fucking clue. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-15-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T10:49:17-08:00","id":830319,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">\u201cThe Bibles we\u2019re working on for computer games are written as if they were texts for a new tabletop edition, and will most likely be released in that format.\u201d</span></b><br /> <br /> I\u2019m getting the impression that they want to stay true to TTRPG roots. They also realize that rainbows and unicorn farts are not going to fund the TTRPG. So, video games.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><b>\u201cThere is only one WoD. Chronicles of Darkness is a sandbox tabletop setting featuring the same broad creature types as the World of Darkness, but it is not the same world. It will not be spun off into computer games, novels, TV or anything else.\u201d</b></span><br /> <br /> I think I see what they\u2019re doing and \u2013 not gonna lie \u2013 I dig it.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">\u201cIf you can write about the Holocaust, you can write about 9/11\u201d</span></b><br /> <br /> Shoah is a wonderful book and proof that something like that can be done tastefully.<br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T10:54:49-08:00","id":830331,"title":"","content":"What wrecked the glorious perfection that was TSR And brought us the catastrophe that was the spellplague, which led to disavowing D&amp;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:15:22-08:00","id":830346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf#post830298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">imagonem.org/2016/02/15/white-wolfs-lead-storyteller-there-will-be-a-release-in-2016/<br /> <br /> I really, really don't like the look of things here; the overly edgy tone, the statement that roleplaying games don't sell and that they'll focus almost entirely on videogames, the insistence that pushing the envelope and doing things like working 9/11 into the fluff are good... this just smacks of a shallow corporate buyout by people who don't have a fucking clue. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree completely. He's right; roleplaying games by and large do not sell. Videogames will be the money make for Paradox, which most people knew going in. The heart and soul(or spirituality as Martin put it) will always be Tabletop. <br /> <br /> I like that they want to push the envelope, and be as creative as they can. No limitations and whatnot. The World of Darkness is in great hands, in my opinion. <br /> <br /> Wonder what the 2016 release will be...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:38:44-08:00","id":830365,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty mixed on it. There's good parts, and bad parts, of the interview. I think Martin's general ideas are in the right direction. However at the same time he's dismissive of a few things. TTRPG don't print money, but if they didn't sell TTRPG only companies wouldn't exist. There are plenty of fans of the WOD that are fans of the CofD And it feels too much like looking at the top of the RPG industry bubble before it burst as if the top of the bubble was the true state of what the market could support.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't feel like Martin completely appreciates how hard it was to make Shoah a good book. Yes, you can do that for other sensitive topics. But it isn't simple. It takes the write authors, and the right dedication to do so. Not giving into fear is one thing. Throwing out 10 insensitive books for every Shoah book is just a shitty record that needs to be considered rationally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:49:58-08:00","id":830378,"title":"","content":"Reading that they don't appear to give a shit about the table top side actually gave me hope. Hope that they'll let Onyx Path continue to do it's thing in both cWoD and CofD (the second seems pretty much confirmed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:37:08-08:00","id":830476,"title":"","content":"Alright, because I'm lazy, I'm going to start by just reposting what I said about this on GiantITP a little while ago<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me, on another forum</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Which game lines do you plan to revive, and when?</b><br /> So what's Onyx Path been doing all this time? Vampire to Mage are ALIIIIVE!!!!<br /> <br /> <b>Will you prioritize computer games, or will we see pen-and-paper soon?</b><br /> Totally called it. For all the reasons given as well.<br /> <br /> <b>There is only one WoD.</b><br /> My copy of Blood and Smoke begs to differ.<br /> <br /> To be honest, in the last month or so I've grown to like the name change, but I'm never going to except that CofD isn't a World of Darkness. Annoyed that CofD won't be getting any computer games though, I really want a Requiem game more than a Masquerade one.<br /> <br /> I do like that CofD is implied to be being left to OPP. I never really liked the first editions, but the second edition games are what I wanted the oWoD to be, full of mystery and horror, instead of horror and face-punching, and I think that OPP has the right idea for how to bring the line forward. Hoping that OPP might be able to own it eventually.<br /> <br /> <b>New metaplot details</b><br /> Interesting. Although I don't like the new Mage direction, I never felt like the Technocracy was able to properly 'win', just to stay as the top dog for a long time. Also, IIRC, in the old metaplot the Technocracy weren't actually winning, as humanity was settling into it's current state instead of the Union's vision. Also not a big fan of the Werewolf details, I think I'll either nab W20 or jump ship to Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <b>Blah blah fantasy is bad stuff</b><br /> Not happy here. Part of what makes CofD such a great game is that it's not afraid to be both fantasy and horror. The dig at urban fantasy is annoying as well, it makes me glad that OPP have decided to embrace the inherent urban fantasy in Scion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also annoyed at no mention of Changeling plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, it's a mix of good (OPP seeming to retain CofD, which I think they do perfectly), bad (this 9/11 thing), and just not interesting (most of it really). Call me ready to stick to my current collection unless I see a massive change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 02-15-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:54:46-08:00","id":830491,"title":"","content":"Please just let the upcoming X20 stuff go unmolested. Please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T14:20:13-08:00","id":830512,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> I haven't done much WOD in a while, and this ... doesn't intrigue me into looking at it again. &quot;Edgy and Dark&quot; isn't my thing any more - I'm not sure it ever really was. Dark - yes, Edgy for the sake of being edgy - no thanks. And this definitely looks like Edgy for the sake of Edgy. Sorry, dude, it's not the 90's any more.<br /> <br /> Ah well. It looks like at least the CoD stuff will stay with OP, which means no actual change for me, since I like Chronicles of Darkness better than the World of Darkness. So I guess I'll keep going as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T19:24:14-08:00","id":830700,"title":"","content":"Weeeeell... I was positively hopeful about the 4th ed so far, but this seriously toned down my enthusiasm. I liked the directions the X20s take with bringing the setting update, almost all of them. I hoped for something similar but with a continued metaplot and better game mechanics, instead it seems like it's nWoD again as maybe it will be a perfectly good game(s), but not the game(s) I falled in love. Especialy the werewolf and mage parts worries me. And I love the gothic-punk aesthetic and always will. Without it, what vampire will be exactly? A game about humanity and politics? We have Requiem, thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm still hoping for a good 4th edition, I will still take a look at it when it comes out, but yet, I'd lost much of my positiveness about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:06:39-08:00","id":830969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=830378#post830378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading that they don't appear to give a shit about the table top side actually gave me hope. Hope that they'll let Onyx Path continue to do it's thing in both cWoD and CofD (the second seems pretty much confirmed).</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get the impression that they don't care for the table top side? As I see it White Wolf will deal with new editions in WoD while Onyx Path can still make nostalgia books, as Martin puts it, that will take place in the 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:34:30-08:00","id":831015,"title":"","content":"Rereading it, and what I'm mainly getting is a lot of hate for what WoD had become by the end of the line. Especially the hate for it being 'escapist urban fantasy' rather than 'artistic horror' (with the implication that the two are vaguely opposed). For extra fun, by what the old white wolf 'got wrong' it's time to remove the vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, wraiths, demons, mummies, Keui-Jin, and even mummies from the WoD (yeah, I know he didn't mean that, but can't I have some fun).<br /> <br /> The only really explicit thing we've gotten is a metaplot that sounds a bit stupid once you get past the vampire section, with a simplification of the Wyrm (which I do not understand, but I don't believe was actually linked with global warming before this, it seemed more of an acid-rain thing to me), a real oversimplification of what technology has done that ignores the fact that the Virtual Adepts would have had a significant boost in power, and what looks like a very heavy-handed approach to shoving in sensitive topics. Also don't like the shift in werewolf attitudes from 'the Imperguim might have been a mistake' to 'ending it was a mistake'.<br /> <br /> I'm getting less hopeful the more I read it, which is a shame as my favourite WoD game, and the one I'd love to see after it's apocalypse, is Changeling: the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T08:02:57-08:00","id":831030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Onyx Path also have a license to produce nostalgia books for the classic WoD settings. These are official but set in the same nebulous \u201deternal nineties\u201d, using the old-school buckets-of-dice-system featured in the original lines. </div> </div> </div>So the new lines won't be using \u201cbuckets of dice\u201d?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm definitely getting a \u201cclassic Trek vs. Abrams Trek\u201d vibe here when they compare their One World of Darkness to the classic World of Darkness; it's concerning me. Though it's possible \u2014 likely, even \u2014 that it's te result of only two heads being in the game at the moment, and once they start bringing in advisors on the various non-Vampire gamelines, they'll get a better handle on what needs to be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-16-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T10:47:52-08:00","id":831136,"title":"","content":"My own version of WoD is more urban fantasy than horror. In fact I use the background from WoD for fantasy campaigns.<br /> <br /> Maybe WoD needs a fantasy world like a noirpunk version of Exalted or Scarred Lands.<br /> <br /> * When to many supernatural creatures are added to the background, the idea of &quot;monster are hidden among us&quot; is more difficult. It is becomes a &quot;jurasic park&quot;for hammer-films monsters. <br /> <br /> * My opinion is the industry of RPGs will change with the future (double page size) flexible tablet computers, like the mobiles changed the music industry. The pdfs will be used more, and maybe we will see NFCs for games. Another option is the hybrid games, arcade videogames with extra &quot;pencil &amp; paper&quot; pdfs.<br /> <br /> * If there are videogames... will see romance scenes like the ones from Dragon Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:00:04-08:00","id":831329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rereading it, and what I'm mainly getting is a lot of hate for what WoD had become by the end of the line. Especially the hate for it being 'escapist urban fantasy' rather than 'artistic horror' (with the implication that the two are vaguely opposed). For extra fun, by what the old white wolf 'got wrong' it's time to remove the vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, wraiths, demons, mummies, Keui-Jin, and even mummies from the WoD (yeah, I know he didn't mean that, but can't I have some fun).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The only really explicit thing we've gotten is a metaplot that sounds a bit stupid once you get past the vampire section, with a simplification of the Wyrm (which I do not understand, but I don't believe was actually linked with global warming before this, it seemed more of an acid-rain thing to me), a real oversimplification of what technology has done that ignores the fact that the Virtual Adepts would have had a significant boost in power, and what looks like a very heavy-handed approach to shoving in sensitive topics. Also don't like the shift in werewolf attitudes from 'the Imperguim might have been a mistake' to 'ending it was a mistake'.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm getting less hopeful the more I read it, which is a shame as my favourite WoD game, and the one I'd love to see after it's apocalypse, is Changeling: the Dreaming.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The relationship between any part of the Wyrm and global warming would probably entail an awful lot of opportunistic greed spirits and the Chulorviah. Unfortunately, the Chulorviah, among other awesome existing hooks, went unmentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=830969#post830969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get the impression that they don't care for the table top side? As I see it White Wolf will deal with new editions in WoD while Onyx Path can still make nostalgia books, as Martin puts it, that will take place in the 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't have smartphones or widespread wireless internet in the 90s, but they're all over the nostalgia editions. Along with current events, too. Trying to stuff those back into the box would be impossible, so we have to come to the conclusion that that statement is throwing everything off significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T20:05:45-08:00","id":831442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=831329#post831329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't have smartphones or widespread wireless internet in the 90s, but they're all over the nostalgia editions. Along with current events, too. Trying to stuff those back into the box would be impossible, so we have to come to the conclusion that that statement is throwing everything off significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Martin made a similar 90s comment in his Tenebrae Noctis presentation. I think he means that the 20th anniversary editions will retain that &quot;90's gaming feel,&quot; whereas he intends to make One World of Darkness &quot;updated to the 21st century.&quot;<br /> <br /> Our mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T01:13:35-08:00","id":831582,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming they are not really familiar with the Anniversary edition books or their followups outside the most general idea. For instance Rage Accross the World introduces a lot of new stories, characters and current content and how the Garou are coping with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:55:03-08:00","id":832044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=830319#post830319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">\u201cIf you can write about the Holocaust, you can write about 9/11\u201d</span></b><br /> <br /> Shoah is a wonderful book and proof that something like that can be done tastefully.<br /> <br /> [/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you bloody serious?!? You can't be, please tell me you're not. <i>Shoah</i> was disgusting crap from cover to cover. It would have been the worst book WW ever put out, if not for <i>Gypsies</i> (And even then it's close).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:54:31-08:00","id":832094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832044#post832044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you bloody serious?!? You can't be, please tell me you're not. <i>Shoah</i> was disgusting crap from cover to cover. It would have been the worst book WW ever put out, if not for <i>Gypsies</i> (And even then it's close).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:00:41-08:00","id":832100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832094#post832094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I'd really like to hear why it was so bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:44:30-08:00","id":832133,"title":"","content":"Well, I read this and I do not like the new direction that White Wolf is heading. It's too edgy for the sake of being edgy, less World of Darkness and more World of Pitch Blackness in my opinion (feel free to disagree with my opinion). And some of us actually like the &quot;escapist urban fantasy&quot; (like me). \u200bSuffice to say, I will be sticking to my old stuff from 1e, 2e, and X20 for now. That and nWoD/Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Still, I wish Martin the best of luck in his endeavors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:48:01-08:00","id":832137,"title":"","content":"In the grim darkness of the modern world there is only edge!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:58:36-08:00","id":832146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832044#post832044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you bloody serious?!? You can't be, please tell me you're not. <i>Shoah</i> was disgusting crap from cover to cover. It would have been the worst book WW ever put out, if not for <i>Gypsies</i> (And even then it's close).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking source, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:35:20-08:00","id":832169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832133#post832133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I read this and I do not like the new direction that White Wolf is heading. It's too edgy for the sake of being edgy, less World of Darkness and more World of Pitch Blackness.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there you have it, folks. WWP has yet to release a SINGLE product, and the lead storyteller has done all of three or four interviews, and minds have already been made up. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:41:36-08:00","id":832174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832133#post832133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I read this and I do not like the new direction that White Wolf is heading. It's too edgy for the sake of being edgy, less World of Darkness and more World of Pitch Blackness in my opinion (feel free to disagree with my opinion). And some of us actually like the &quot;escapist urban fantasy&quot; (like me). \u200bSuffice to say, I will be sticking to my old stuff from 1e, 2e, and X20 for now. That and nWoD/Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Still, I wish Martin the best of luck in his endeavors.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a personal taste thing, so I respect your opinion. I just don't like how edgy has been thrown around a lot in the (admittedly many) topics discussing the interview. It's not edgy to say that, for example, it's much riskier to use Dementation in downtown Athens because half of the people residing there are already contemplating suicide.<br /> <br /> Or that walking through certain parts of Glasgow while wearing a suit (like the good Ventrue you are) will probably result in a stab, final death, and run scenario. You would regret celebrating Maggie's victory back in the 1980s, if you didn't truly believe that it's their fault they (or their parents, more likely) didn't adapt to a changing economy. How hard is it for a 40+ y.o. shipyard worker to go to uni and study Finance, after all?<br /> <br /> Urban heroism and escapism is all fine and well, and I enjoy the occasional break of writing up such a chronicle. But does it <i>really</i> sound like you guys need a metaplot for superheroes with fangs? Aren't those stories more about the characters anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 02-17-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:39:20-08:00","id":832228,"title":"","content":"I do not like the statement about Urban Fantasy. Changeling: the Dreaming and Mage: The Asension are both urban fantasy with shades of horror. that is how they were presented from the get go. to turn mage into a straight up horror story and you loose a huge part of what the game is about. Restoring wonder and magic to the world is what the Kithian and the Traditions<b> DO</b>. I can see it for Vampire, Werewolf and Wraith, but Changeling and Mage are Urban Fantasy games and a huge part of what draws me to them om in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:13:34-08:00","id":832247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832228#post832228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not like the statement about Urban Fantasy. Changeling: the Dreaming and Mage: The Asension are both urban fantasy with shades of horror. that is how they were presented from the get go. to turn mage into a straight up horror story and you loose a huge part of what the game is about. Restoring wonder and magic to the world is what the Kithian and the Traditions<b> DO</b>. I can see it for Vampire, Werewolf and Wraith, but Changeling and Mage are Urban Fantasy games and a huge part of what draws me to them om in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, Mage does make itself the odd one out by 1) not having actual monsters of even scant familiarity as its main thing (witches don't really feel like a specific type of monster, and even so, Mage would be farther away from them than Werewolf is from Lon Chaney) and 2) having setting assumptions that are very difficult to incorporate into the settings of other games, like Consensus and technology being a type of magic(k).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:38:43-08:00","id":832272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832247#post832247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, Mage does make itself the odd one out by 1) not having actual monsters of even scant familiarity as its main thing (witches don't really feel like a specific type of monster, and even so, Mage would be farther away from them than Werewolf is from Lon Chaney) and 2) having setting assumptions that are very difficult to incorporate into the settings of other games, like Consensus and technology being a type of magic(k).</div> </div> </div> </div>Be that as it may, turning Mage into a straight up horror story is still a major compromise of it's themes and mood. It's a certainly a dark urban fantasy with strong elements of horror, but it is first and foremost an urban fantasy setting rather than a horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T21:53:20-08:00","id":832321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832169#post832169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there you have it, folks. WWP has yet to release a SINGLE product, and the lead storyteller has done all of three or four interviews, and minds have already been made up.</div> </div> </div> </div>If those three or four interviews didn't have specific statements on the direction the lead storyteller wants to take the game, maybe minds wouldn't be made up. But thankfully he <i><b>has </b></i>made those specific statements about where he wants to bring the game. Now we, the consumers, can start making decisions about a product that increasingly sounds less interesting to a few of us.<br /> <br /> The assumption that we should wait and see what the finished product looks like is a nice thought and all, but if the trailer of a movie doesn't look interesting at all, I doubt I'm missing much by not seeing it. This is the same situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T00:48:30-08:00","id":832382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832272#post832272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be that as it may, turning Mage into a straight up horror story is still a major compromise of it's themes and mood. It's a certainly a dark urban fantasy with strong elements of horror, but it is first and foremost an urban fantasy setting rather than a horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Although again, I hold my reservations regarding what the interview <i>actually</i> meant, but I definitely don't want to see Mage turned into Vampire with spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:05:27-08:00","id":832398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832228#post832228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not like the statement about Urban Fantasy. Changeling: the Dreaming and Mage: The Asension are both urban fantasy with shades of horror. that is how they were presented from the get go. to turn mage into a straight up horror story and you loose a huge part of what the game is about. Restoring wonder and magic to the world is what the Kithian and the Traditions<b> DO</b>. I can see it for Vampire, Werewolf and Wraith, but Changeling and Mage are Urban Fantasy games and a huge part of what draws me to them om in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is very little Gothic about Werewolf. There is a lot of Punk, and stuff like magical hobo guardians of the downtrodden trafficking with strange gods and spirits in the back allies of the world, or legendary heroes on quests across impossible realms to save their own world.. So, yeah, Urban Fantasy does spring to mind. Martin seems to think that it's a badword, though. Considering the impact of Young Adult fiction on the Urban Fantasy genre in the past decade I can see how he can think that. But Neil Gaiman also writes Urban Fantasy, and that's on cue for most WoD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:09:37-08:00","id":832399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832044#post832044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you bloody serious?!? You can't be, please tell me you're not. <i>Shoah</i> was disgusting crap from cover to cover. It would have been the worst book WW ever put out, if not for <i>Gypsies</i> (And even then it's close).</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain that? I've found it to be a horrible book in so far that it's<b> really</b> hard to read and talks quite plainly about horrors of man and how they seep into the dreams and nightmares of people who lost their lives. I've also found it well researched, well thought out and respectful.<br /> <br /> So I'm curious how you can compare it to the book about magical misunderstood blood magician thieves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:57:07-08:00","id":832412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832398#post832398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is very little Gothic about Werewolf. There is a lot of Punk, and stuff like magical hobo guardians of the downtrodden trafficking with strange gods and spirits in the back allies of the world, or legendary heroes on quests across impossible realms to save their own world.. So, yeah, Urban Fantasy does spring to mind. Martin seems to think that it's a badword, though. Considering the impact of Young Adult fiction on the Urban Fantasy genre in the past decade I can see how he can think that. But Neil Gaiman also writes Urban Fantasy, and that's on cue for most WoD games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the tribes prefer a rural setting though! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, I've seen people steer away from explicitly calling Gaiman's works urban fantasy, but that's because they prefer to highlight the fact he's slightly more mythological than most Urban Fantasy authors. But still exactly what I thought the World of Darkness would be, down to Neverwhere being about an enchanted mortal. I seem to be getting an idea from the interview that the only 'darkness' that is 'dark' enough for the World of Darkness is once all the light has been turned off. I hereby suggest <a href=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/vsbattles/images/a/a3/Black-windows_542931.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20150317090032\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as the new page design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T07:23:25-08:00","id":832509,"title":"","content":"A very big mansion in a far rural region like the one from the movie &quot;Crimson Peaks&quot; also may be really gothic<br /> <br /> * The garous are too &quot;epic&quot; to be characters from horror genre. They are like cartoon furry heroes for adult fanboys. Changeling: dreaming was too anti-gothic, but now changeling: the lost is enough gothic. Wraith was too dark-gothic. I would rather to use wraiths for crossover allies. Who wants to play a sad wraith when you can be a mummy? About the demons.. there were too newbie, noobs, new arrival or newcomer. Powerful, but added in the last time. <br /> <br /> * For a remake of gypsies my suggestion is &quot;cosmopolitan nomad clans&quot;,<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T07:44:13-08:00","id":832516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832509#post832509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The garous are too &quot;epic&quot; to be characters from horror genre. They are like cartoon furry heroes for adult fanboys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. I'm sure there is no horror in fighting a battle you cannot win, putting everything you love in danger of dying horribly from you and listening to the swansong of the world you were meant to protect. You might actually want to read up on Werewolf before making such clueless sweeping statements.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:41:50-08:00","id":832561,"title":"","content":"Are we reading too much about this &quot;urban fantasy&quot; commentary ? It seems to me that he hated the tedious link between the WoD and Exalted hinted mainly by some early Hunter sourcebook and the apocryphia at the begining of Laws of Ascension collector's edition.<br /> For the rest, he clearly wants the &quot;punk&quot; back big time in the mood of the game. We'll see how it all works out went the first product will be released.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:20:23-08:00","id":832577,"title":"","content":"Garous may be failed or tragic heroes, but too epic to be &quot;gothic&quot;. They don't know about the sacrifice will be worth, but they are going to try, al least they will die like true warrior, fighting with courage and sacrifice, nor hidden and waiting the death. And I create my own stories about hope, not about nihilism. I don't mind the canon background, I will give an oportunity for a happy end, or at least suvivors to start again. <br /> <br /> I love the bet\u00e9 or shapeshipter races (bastest, annanasi, ratkin, mokole..) but they are further from ghotic-punk. They are more like &quot;neo-tribal metal&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com