forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833121#post833121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, I should put this in my signature, [color=blue]blue[/blue] means sarcasm in my posts. I was just making fun of what I see as embracing the worst of cWoD, including crossovers (therefore, Haight).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm used to lavender meaning sarcasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:08:44-08:00","id":833226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=832788#post832788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the mailmen will be issued trench coats and katanas to wear while delivering the POD copies.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800080\">Of course. How else would they destroy your old books to force you play the new, correct edition?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:42:45-08:00","id":833307,"title":"","content":"Lot of &quot;sky is falling&quot; proclamations in here and people seeming to read everything in the interview the worst way possible. He wasn't saying ttrpgs sold for shit, he was saying nWoD did, and he is right. The move to nWoD killed White Wolf. <br /> <br /> I for one am looking forward to what they are going to put out and hope we get something earlier than later so I can work the metaplot events of 2002-2016 into my chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:44:40-08:00","id":833309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833101#post833101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2082\" data-vbnamecard=\"2082\">Schleiermacher</a> is coming back guys</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell- a troll that refuses to be fed? I have been wearing my special internet-fighting underpants for two days, dammit!<br /> <br /> And you expect me to be mollified with with a WOD full of blackjack and hookers? I can get that from any children's card game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:24:59-08:00","id":833402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833309#post833309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What the hell- a troll that refuses to be fed? I have been wearing my special internet-fighting underpants for two days, dammit!<br /> <br /> And you expect me to be mollified with with a WOD full of blackjack and hookers? I can get that from any children's card game!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you remembered your adult diaper, too. That's a long time to sit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:38:44-08:00","id":833410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833307#post833307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lot of &quot;sky is falling&quot; proclamations in here and people seeming to read everything in the interview the worst way possible. He wasn't saying ttrpgs sold for shit, he was saying nWoD did, and he is right. The move to nWoD killed White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of charity for Martin's comments is because this is growing into a repeated pattern with him. Even when he has a point, he phrases it in a poor way, wraps it in a bunch of stuff that upsets the primary North American market for the games, and then has to do damage control. The problem is it's already gotten bad enough that the damage control itself furthers &quot;sky is falling&quot; feelings rather than actually mollifying people.<br /> <br /> And no, the move to the CofD didn't kill White Wolf. The CCP acquisition of White Wolf did, because CCP seriously mishandled the IP (without even successfully producing the game they bought it to make). As OPP has shown, the CofD sells well enough to support its continued existence in the right hands. Martin isn't even saying this anyway. He's saying that the CofD never went gangbusters like the WoD did (but neglects the completely different markets and cultural factors behind this), and that if the CofD had done in 2004, what WoD did in 1991, CofD would be the focus on WWP's future plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:06:16-08:00","id":833435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833307#post833307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lot of &quot;sky is falling&quot; proclamations in here and people seeming to read everything in the interview the worst way possible. He wasn't saying ttrpgs sold for shit, he was saying nWoD did, and he is right. The move to nWoD killed White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's quite that bad, at least yet. It's certainly put me off enough that I won't buy the new editions without first looking at the metaplot and the implied new mechanical system, because I have no guarantee that either will be my taste.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, part of the original problem with nWoD was it was still too routed in the cWoD. Requiem especially smelt like 'Masquerade but simplified' rather than the rather interesting game it actually is. Now I don't think Requiem 2e would have done any better for WW if it had been released as the first nWoD game, but ten years down the line and rebranded as CofD (which sounds like a better name the more I hear it) it's got it's own audience and is going strong, enough so that there was legitimate concern from a few people that it would be cancelled or merged with the cWoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I for one am looking forward to what they are going to put out and hope we get something earlier than later so I can work the metaplot events of 2002-2016 into my chronicle. </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem for me is that I was legitimately interested in OPP's V4. The bits revealed seemed to me like an attempt to stay in continuity, but move back towards a 1e/early 2e feel, which I liked although I acknowledge that some people might not, and using Gehenna as a sort of semi-reboot to refocus the game and change vampires slightly (I suspect one of the changes would be a reworking of the link between generation and strength).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:44:53-08:00","id":833612,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oh boy. I apologise for making a drive-by instead of substantiating my comments, I am genuinely surprised they would be that controversial.<br /> <br /> I will admit that the comparison to <i>Gypsies</i> was hyperbolic and unwarranted, but while it's not quite <i>that</i> bad I absolutely maintain that <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i> is exploitative, ill-considered, in extremely poor taste and without merit.<br /> <br /> I did not comment to that effect to troll, and I especially resent the assumption from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"164\" data-vbnamecard=\"164\">Malcolm</a> that I don't know what I'm talking about. I own the book, I have read it in full (including the foreword) and while I wasn't aware that Jonathan Blacke was Jewish, the best that allows me to say about the book is that presumably it was created with no malicious intent. If you like it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"164\" data-vbnamecard=\"164\">Malcolm</a>, then defend it like an adult.<br /> <br /> <b>Here are my criticisms in full:</b><br /> <br /> First and least of all, the language used throughout the book is overwrought and blatantly manipulative, in a way that the subject matter absolutely does not need and which only does it a disservice. At times it shades so far into the purple as to become outright disgusting, as when it's written that \u00abThe killings [at Auschwitz] started slowly, tentatively, like a new lover\u2019s first bashful caresses.\u00bb What the Hell is that? Thus, while clearly meticulously researched the book still fails when considered as a textbook.<br /> <br /> How about as a game book?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, in what I presume to be an effort to avoid trivializing the Holocaust, the writer has gone too far in the other direction, exceptionalizing its perpetrators, victims, context and fallout in a way that makes no sense from an in-game perspective. The bulk of the fictional material within the book is taken up with a description of the calamitous effects of the arrival of twelve million camp-dead Enfants in the Shadowlands -an entirely unprecedented number.<br /> <br /> Except it's not. More people died over a similar time frame in World War I, 25 years prior, fully half as many in just one year during the Holodomor. Of course, probably fewer of those became Wraiths... but even that ignores that while the Holocaust was ongoing, so was World War II, which killed at least 50 million people worldwide <i>outside </i>of the death camps. If the logistical challenge of the Holocaust revolutionized Stygian society, World War II should have drowned it in chaos.<br /> <br /> And hang on. <i><i>Every single</i> </i>victim of the death camps became a Wraith? Well, yes, of course. It would have been impossible to write the book in any other way, an insult to every victim whose rage or regret or connection to their next of kin was deemed \u00abnot strong enough\u00bb by the writer... but this should have been the first of many blazing signposts to White Wolf that this book should never have been written, because it is as absurd from an in-universe perspective as it is necessary from a real-word perspective, and an insult to all other victims of human evil and their relatives. <i><i>Wraith</i> </i>and real, murdered people do not mix.<br /> <br /> Besides, for all its protestations of preserving the memories of twelve million <i><i>individuals</i>,</i> this book treats the ghostly victims of the Holocaust as a homogenous mass defined entirely by their victimhood and the circumstances of their deaths.<br /> <br /> This takes its most grotesque form in the descriptions of the free camps \u2013 which the text refers to as \u00abghettos\u00bb more often than not, in an intensely tone-deaf choice of words: The twelve million Holocaust dead are granted freedom and sovereignity over the Shadowlands sites of the <i>camps and execution grounds where they were killed</i>. Who would suggest that? Who would accept it? And who could possibly think it was a good idea to write, without seeing how dehumanizing it is? While some of the camp-dead would probably have enough Angst that the nightmarish reminders of their torturous deaths suited their temperaments and tastes, when you write something like this you have to consider that what kept these people clinging close to life -their Fetters, in other words- would absolutely not be limited to the indignities of the last days of their lives \u2013 they had relatives, memories and unfinished business from tens of millions of places all over Europe and the world; they will want to do almost as many different things as there are people.<br /> <br /> It's not only the victims of the Holocaust who are tarred with a broad brush by the book, but the perpetrators as well -when they are mentioned at all. It's by all means <i>understandable</i> that the ghosts of German soldiers and government officials do not receive a lot of attention in a book about their primary victims, but it is still unfortunate -all the more so because a book purporting to cover themes of individual heroism and culpability, guilt, forgiveness and redemption declines at any point to consider that a Nazi soldier or SS-man who became a Wraith probably didn't cling to life out of an unfulfilled desire to persecute Jews some more. At every turn they are presented as nothing but the most one-dimensionally evil of acceptable targets.<br /> <br /> The decision to paper over all this diversity with the ersatz post-mortem Israel of the free camps, complete with international criticism and prejudice, hunts for \u00abescaped\u00bb Nazi ghosts and mystically significant \u00abNever Forget\u00bb- sentiments (that are entirely incongruous with the presentation of relics, fetters and Harrowing elsewhere in <i>Wraith</i>) not only rings entirely false and leaves a foul taste in the mouth as written, but could not possibly manage to do otherwise. The sensibilities of writer and audience both quite understandably demand some kind of redemptive spin on the tragedy, a constructive reaction that suggests we can learn from it and in the future, rise above the hate and evil that caused it \u2013 but using <i>Wraith</i> as a vehicle for this message renders it off-putting and saccharine. It only highlights again how unsuitable the Holocaust is as subject material for a fantasy RPG, however dark in tone and maturely presented -the conflicting demands of the topic and the genre are irreconcilable. The write-ups and references given in the later sections of the book to those characters who were actual historical people further underline this \u2013 no, I do not want to make a game of hunting down the ghost of Mengele and welding it into a portal of screaming Auschwitz personel as the capstone to a latter-day Gate of Hell. The idea is obscene.<br /> <br /> It's not the only obscenity in the location write-ups either \u2013 the Auschwitz chapter in particular is rife with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The [crematoriums], though hated and dreaded in equal measure, are </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> vital components of the camp\u2019s economy. Here, in these infernos, legions of monstrous dybbuks toil, soulforging Corpora and wire into needed goods for use or barter. Never is the vicinity free from the blast of the ovens, the roar of the flames and the screams of the molten. </div> </div> </div>So the victims become the victimizers, in an eternal parody of the way they died. Lovely. Now in the context of <i>Wraith</i> this is indisputably an idea that <i>makes sense</i>, and arguably even makes for great horror- but again -that just highlights the impossibility of reconciling a respectful treatment of the Holocaust with the demands of good game material -I shouldn't have to belabor how far this excerpt is from being the former.<br /> <br /> I wrote this in a style that's primarily focused on in-game material, I realize, and I hope that it is not too off-putting or flippant of me to do so, as my criticism applies to both an in-game and out-of-game perspective on the way the book portrays Holocaust victims -it is a testament to the skill of the writers of <i>Wraith</i> that I feel I can confidently leave the real-world corollaries of the in-game criticisms to those of you who read this to follow.<br /> <br /> I hope those of you who asked me to clarify my position over the past few days find some value in this explanation.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","user":"Schleiermacher","date":". 02-19-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:14:53-08:00","id":834144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833612#post833612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the victims become the victimizers, in an eternal parody of the way they died. Lovely. Now in the context of <i>Wraith</i> this is indisputably an idea that <i>makes sense</i>, and arguably even makes for great horror- but again -that just highlights the impossibility of reconciling a respectful treatment of the Holocaust with the demands of good game material -I shouldn't have to belabor how far this excerpt is from being the former.<br /> <br /> I wrote this in a style that's primarily focused on in-game material, I realize, and I hope that it is not too off-putting or flippant of me to do so, as my criticism applies to both an in-game and out-of-game perspective on the way the book portrays Holocaust victims -it is a testament to the skill of the writers of <i>Wraith</i> that I feel I can confidently leave the real-world corollaries of the in-game criticisms to those of you who read this to follow.<br /> <br /> I hope those of you who asked me to clarify my position over the past few days find some value in this explanation.[/SIZE][/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this. It's a rather well thought out critique compared to the first statement. I still believe you may have judged it too harshly, as this is what Wraith is about. You yourself have noticed that this makes sense within the context of Wraith, and the thing with giant influxes of dead is not endemic to just the Holocaust - The Great War has quite a bit to say about the dead influx, as does commentary on the Black Plagues and the Spanish Influenza. Of course the result is dark, twisted and disturbing, of course that the camps become dark mirrors. However it's noteable that not all Germans are the enemy in that book, and that not all germans are nazis, as not all of the victims are hunters, also a closer reading of the book points out it's not that everyone becomes a Wraith, it's just that suffering tends to produce more Wraiths then msot other things.<br /> <br /> It's what Wraith does and why the book has a warning about the content is within it. It's the kind of game that forces you to deal with echoes of lives lost and the consequences of human actions. I can agree that it's a disturbing book, but I still feel that it deals with the content with a lot more tact and forethought than most WW books. Better yet, it actually presents something that's actually a major point in Wraith. Comparing it with the racist caricature that was Gypsies is just... wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:39:31-08:00","id":834293,"title":"","content":"Well, butter my biscuit. That was about as well-reasoned a response as I could ask for.<br /> <br /> I did not wear my arguin' pants for nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=833612#post833612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the victims become the victimizers, in an eternal parody of the way they died. Lovely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asmodai already posted a bang-up response, but this line in particular stuck out to me. Now, I don't want to get political or anything here, but arguably the savagery with which the Jews were treated during the Holocaust caused some of the <i>living </i>victims to in turn become victimizers. A reporter for the Daily Telegraph spoke of the ardently Zionist Irgun's tactics in 1948 and likened their fear-mongering brutality to the very Nazis some of their members had fought:<br /> <br /> &quot;(The) Irgun (are) in fact rapidly becoming the 'SS' of the new state. There is also a strong 'Gestapo' \u2013 but no-one knows who is in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, the Irgun did some distasteful stuff even before the war, but clearly abuse has a cyclical nature. I don't think it was improper of White Wolf to depict that on the other side of the Shroud... it does not demean those who died, or lessen the horror of their suffering.<br /> <br /> If anything, telling stories (even ghost stories) about those who suffered in the Holocaust keeps the memory of them alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-21-2016, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T03:52:13-08:00","id":835668,"title":"","content":"The expressed disdain for urban fantasy is disappointing, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:10:46-08:00","id":835741,"title":"","content":"About controversial threads my advice is the authors should be careful, because sometimes the reader feels to be like a war veteran hearing stupy advices by a wargames and FPS videogames fanboy. For example an author writes a story about hate, conflict and predjudices, and then a reader says &quot;don't preach me about intolerance and fanatism if you have fogorten to teach respecting the human dignity&quot;. To teach about History or current real world conflicts isn't so easy if the reader thinks he knows more than you about certain matters. <br /> <br /> If people are offended or molested, they don't worry about what do you think about the right limits, they will complain, because &quot;their&quot; rules aren't like yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:14:18-08:00","id":836110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=835668#post835668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The expressed disdain for urban fantasy is disappointing, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember, English isn't the guy's first language. He could have just as easily meant something like the &quot;Vampire D&amp;D&quot; playstyle most of us are not keen on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:51:03-08:00","id":836122,"title":"","content":"He could have but I'm going to go with &quot;he meant what he said&quot; until he says differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 02-23-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T01:01:31-08:00","id":836290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=836110#post836110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, English isn't the guy's first language. He could have just as easily meant something like the &quot;Vampire D&amp;D&quot; playstyle most of us are not keen on.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is Swedish and came from management of a global gaming company. His English is better than many Americans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:00:45-08:00","id":837723,"title":"","content":"It is perhaps worth noting that the job posting on the Paradox Interactive website for an editor for White Wolf does stipulate English language skills among other things... They further want someone knowledgeable about the various White Wolf/World of Darkness games' systems, and someone who can act as a lead to express their vision of their One World of Darkness. Oh, also this is only the third position they show for White Wolf Publishing on their website, after Tobias and Martin. It kinda makes me think they're still looking into what exactly they want and where exactly they want to go.<br /> <br /> As for the statements, I'm willing to chalk them up to Martin attempting to speak to the 'base' of fans, and it's possible he doesn't know who that base is. Rather, I mean that <i>we</i> here on these boards may not be his intended audience, or at least we are not his <i>specific</i> audience. We all know how wonderful and powerful tabletop RPGs are, but as I've followed the Paradox Interactive acquisition of White Wolf across these interwebs, I've seen a LOT of gamers of, uh let's call it 'other stripes' (i.e. videogamers) commenting on various sites' coverage. It could be Martin looking to get those who are 'on the fence' or those who just outright don't know anything about tabletop RPGs to give it a look.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's good or bad (totes feel free to let me know if that's how you read this), but I count myself among those who've seen the White Wolf properties go through all kinds of changes in the past decades. I have faith that this version will more likely be good than be a disaster. I haven't been wrong yet, but of course there IS always a first time for everything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T17:01:57-08:00","id":837815,"title":"","content":"Granted, the Silent Striders did touch on 9-11 and handled it well, I'm not too worried about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:19:09-08:00","id":838260,"title":"","content":"Here's a new one...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.worldofdarkness.news/Articles/tabid/95/Article/13/WoD-News-interview-with-White-Wolf-Martin-Elricsson.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.worldofdarkness.news/Articles/tabid/95/Article/13/WoD-News-interview-with-White-Wolf-Martin-Elricsson.aspx\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.worldofdarkness.news/Articles/tabid/95/Article/13/WoD-News-interview-with-White-Wolf-Martin-Elricsson.aspx\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.worldofdarkness.news/Articles/tabid/95/Article/13/WoD-News-interview-with-White-Wolf-Martin-Elricsson.aspx </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:35:06-08:00","id":838267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are involved in approval and adjusting some minor things to hint at what is to come and make V20 compatible with future changes. </div> </div> </div>This is the part where I bitch about my thread getting deleted regarding rumors of Paradox asking for V20 flavor changes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But overall, this interview is much less abrasive than the previous one and made me like this pair quite a bit more; Martin sounds less like an edgy bastard and more like a fan of both White Wolf's works (CofD included!) and thr wider tabletop community, which is a relief. I've got massive respect for anyone who can love Trail of Cthulhu as well, which hopefully indicates that he's willing to let V4 modernize the ruleset somewhat. While I'm still not sold on all this, the change in tone and the clear interest in what Onyx Path go a long way towards winning me over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-27-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:44:36-08:00","id":838273,"title":"","content":"It's... interesting. I hope this means Gehenna hasn't finished.<br /> <br /> Otherwise a few things that I don't really care about, the almost deal-breaking implication of a strong metaplot, no mention of any non-vampire games, and so on. Only one thing that stood out to me as a red flag, but nothing really that makes me hopeful. I've got no idea where V4 will be thematically, are we going back to Elders versus Anarchs, A Beast I Am Lest A Beast I Become, or somewhere else entirely? I am even more confused as to what the state of the rules will be, and I'm sure anything without a bucket of d10s being required will cause a split in the fanbase.<br /> <br /> In fact, I see a lot of potential for the fanbase to split. It's already split on metaplot, which nWW seems to be focusing on, and I can see the pro-metaplot side being split on the quality of the new metaplot.<br /> <br /> Also, based on these, I think Vampire is being focused on almost exclusively. Which doesn't surprise me, I saw this as inevitable, but it's still sad that it might take a long time for the other games to get anything, and I've seen nothing for those that aren't the 'big 3'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:51:15-08:00","id":838277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=838273#post838273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, based on these, I think Vampire is being focused on almost exclusively. Which doesn't surprise me, I saw this as inevitable, but it's still sad that it might take a long time for the other games to get anything, and I've seen nothing for those that aren't the 'big 3'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even barring the fact that VtM is kinda the face of the World of Darkness, he addresses this in the interview in way that satisfies me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me 5 years of V20 is starting to look like a complete edition of Vampire. Werewolf and Mage have some way to go. </div> </div> </div>W20 has what has a handful of supplements out. M20 has literally one. Wr20 and C20 haven't even released yet. Why would White Wolf focus on new editions for games that barely exist in the previous? It looks like they're treating X20 as a step between Revised their proposed 4th, and that's fine by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:32:24-08:00","id":838338,"title":"","content":"He also said that they would be doing the other games in previous interviews, though I doubt they'll even consider a timetable for them until after V4 launches and they have time to see the reactions to it.<br /> <br /> As one of the pro-metaplot people I'm super excited. That's one of the major draws of WoD for me and it's something those that don't like it can always ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:43:46-08:00","id":839026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=838277#post838277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even barring the fact that VtM is kinda the face of the World of Darkness, he addresses this in the interview in way that satisfies me:</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I understand exactly why they are focusing on Vampire, it's just annoying to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W20 has what has a handful of supplements out. M20 has literally one. Wr20 and C20 haven't even released yet. Why would White Wolf focus on new editions for games that barely exist in the previous? It looks like they're treating X20 as a step between Revised their proposed 4th, and that's fine by me. </div> </div> </div>Going by the X20s, that still leaves Hunter and Demon, both of which have not had new editions announced, and Demon at the least needs a serious explanation of what the metaplot's been up to this past decade. Vampire might be the face of the World of Darkness, but it's also the one that will likely change the most with the new metaplot (compared to Werewolf and Mage just being made 'darker and edgier'), which could be a make or break deal for several people (to start with, if Gehenna has come and the Tremere haven't died in a shower of blood I won't be buying the game at all). I have a feeling Vampire is being focused on first because Vampire is the game that is released first (which is also why it's probably the face of WoD), although that just might be me reading too much into stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:30:49-08:00","id":839249,"title":"","content":"Vampire is the firstborn child, and the superstar. And today vampires are the favorite ones for the supernatural romance books.<br /> <br /> I suggest some retcons, the mummies, demons and hunter like &quot;veterans&quot;, not like the &quot;new arrival&quot; ones from the previous edition. Why not demons and hunters in the dark age?<br /> <br /> * Now I am thinking,..... if there are Indian kue-jins (oriental vampires).... is it possible &quot;western kue-jins&quot; from Indian people who travelled toward Europe? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:52:18-08:00","id":839261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=839249#post839249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is the firstborn child, and the superstar. And today vampires are the favorite ones for the supernatural romance books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet there are so many good ideas in other games that it seems a shame to put so much into Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suggest some retcons, the mummies, demons and hunter like &quot;veterans&quot;, not like the &quot;new arrival&quot; ones from the previous edition. Why not demons and hunters in the dark age?<br /> <br /> * Now I am thinking,..... if there are Indian kue-jins (oriental vampires).... is it possible &quot;western kue-jins&quot; from Indian people who travelled toward Europe?<br /> </div> </div> </div>South Asian Hungry Dead were noted in KotE as far back as its core and continued being a thing, particularly in regard to the Infinite Thunders Court. However, people from outside of Asia still don't end up as Hungry Dead at this juncture, because of some deal with paradigms of death from Wraith. Also, &quot;oriental&quot; is a rather loaded term to use in description, none the least of which because it's maddeningly vague and could refer to anything from Eastern Europe to the Middle East to Indonesia. From there, it goes into a crappy train of thought that paints everything to the east of Europe as &quot;exotic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T05:31:03-08:00","id":839820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=835668#post835668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The expressed disdain for urban fantasy is disappointing, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see disdain, he's saying that he believes that the World of Darkness' unique element among modern supernatural settings is that it was horror rather than urban fantasy. Now, you can argue that premise (genre definitions are tricky things and the lines are often blurry), but I think it is unfair to read into it that he's putting down urban fantasy. A good parallel, for me, is folks who don't like the new Sherlock Holmes movies because they are action films. This doesn't necessarily mean that they hate action films, just that they don't think the tone fits those particular stories.<br /> <br /> In this case, I think he has a point. Stuff like Dresden Files or Buffy have horrific elements but the tone isn't horror. Buffy and Harry don't ever react in horror to dealing with creatures that prey off of humanity by consuming their blood and treating them like cattle, they fight them the same way that Indiana Jones fights Nazis. Part of the uniqueness of Vampire was that it acknowledged the horror of what vampires were and expected the PCs to do so as well. You aren't just superheroes that happen to get their power-ups from drinking blood, you are predators preying on humanity, leeches on society in a literal sense. Granted, not all games (hell maybe most games) didn't really explore this, but it was a unique aspect of the game. You are playing monsters, with the stress on MONSTERS. That's what I think he's looking to reclaim.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just my opinion on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T09:52:37-08:00","id":839983,"title":"","content":"This is the internet age, now people don't spend money to buy rpg books about fluff but they want crunch. When we want ideas about background we search wikis of videogames, teleseries, novels. The rpg books are like building toys. You buy the box but after you create what your want.<br /> <br /> Some players wants supernatural soap-operas/romances, anothers survival horror, and somebody horror+action about kicking-ass monsters. I don't respect the canon at all but I would rather creating crazy mash-up mixing things from different IPs (= Intelectual Property)/franchises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:29:40-08:00","id":840006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=839983#post839983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the internet age, now people don't spend money to buy rpg books about fluff but they want crunch. When we want ideas about background we search wikis of videogames, teleseries, novels. The rpg books are like building toys. You buy the box but after you create what your want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Stats and weird powers are easy to crib, I want a well-thought out world to put my players into. I really enjoyed 'fluff' only books like the Horror Recognition Guide, and most of the tribe and clanbooks are geared more towards setting and story than rules. Dozens of pages of background and a couple of pages of new gifts/disciplines and rites/merits. <br /> <br /> Using the wikis for background isn't even scratching the surface in most cases. That is how you end up with a shallow understanding of the setting and before you know it all your Get of Fenris are howling Nazi vikings and your Malkavians all start to taste like fish.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:59:37-08:00","id":840120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=840006#post840006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Stats and weird powers are easy to crib, I want a well-thought out world to put my players into. I really enjoyed 'fluff' only books like the Horror Recognition Guide, and most of the tribe and clanbooks are geared more towards setting and story than rules. Dozens of pages of background and a couple of pages of new gifts/disciplines and rites/merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Did you ever try the Mythos Dossiers for the Laundry? It's an amazing source with 140 pages of fluff and setting ideas with what the monsters are up to, and 4 pages of rules. It even got an Ennie!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:08:50-08:00","id":840232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=839820#post839820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are playing monsters, with the stress on MONSTERS. That's what I think he's looking to reclaim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that might work for Vampire (and to a good extent Werewolf), but that doesn't quite work so well for the other games. If I had to explain what the Darkness was in each of the WoD games I'd go for something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Horror/Monstrosity<br /> Werewolf: Horror/Monstrosity<br /> Mage: Opression<br /> Changeling: inevitability<br /> Wraith: hopelessness<br /> Hunter: Horror/Monstrosity, but from the other side compared to Vampire<br /> Demon: really not sure, it's there, and certainly not horror because there's far less inevitability about it (it's far easier for a demon to be good)<br /> <br /> So, I'm pretty much fine with the focus on Horror for Vampire. But if it seeps into my Mage, Changeling, and Demon, I'll be highly annoyed. I mean, I don't even see the horror as the draw for vampire, in there it's the political gameplay and the plots that made me interested, although I like the idea of 'A Beast I Am Lest A Beast I Become'.<br /> <br /> So yeah, V4 probably doesn't look like a game for me, unless it includes a good mechanical system, political plotting, and an absence of Tremere. But I'll certainly glance at Mage if it retains part of that wonder and Urban Fantasy that made the game for me. Mage isn't a horror story, if anything it's a dystopia story.<br /> <br /> Also, definitely agreeing on buying books for fluff. I don't personally do it much, but I've had cases of buying books just to translate the fluff to a different system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:51:59-08:00","id":840286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=840232#post840232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, that might work for Vampire (and to a good extent Werewolf), but that doesn't quite work so well for the other games. If I had to explain what the Darkness was in each of the WoD games I'd go for something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Horror/Monstrosity<br /> Werewolf: Horror/Monstrosity<br /> Mage: Opression<br /> Changeling: inevitability<br /> Wraith: hopelessness<br /> Hunter: Horror/Monstrosity, but from the other side compared to Vampire<br /> Demon: really not sure, it's there, and certainly not horror because there's far less inevitability about it (it's far easier for a demon to be good)<br /> <br /> So, I'm pretty much fine with the focus on Horror for Vampire. But if it seeps into my Mage, Changeling, and Demon, I'll be highly annoyed. I mean, I don't even see the horror as the draw for vampire, in there it's the political gameplay and the plots that made me interested, although I like the idea of 'A Beast I Am Lest A Beast I Become'.<br /> <br /> So yeah, V4 probably doesn't look like a game for me, unless it includes a good mechanical system, political plotting, and an absence of Tremere. But I'll certainly glance at Mage if it retains part of that wonder and Urban Fantasy that made the game for me. Mage isn't a horror story, if anything it's a dystopia story.<br /> <br /> Also, definitely agreeing on buying books for fluff. I don't personally do it much, but I've had cases of buying books just to translate the fluff to a different system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. One of Mage 20's best statements for me that &quot;you are not helpless, you have power, you can change the world!&quot;. I like different tones, i like the existential horror of vampire, also like the political/mystical aspect. I'm not much interested in an all &quot; just dark and gloom and end of the world&quot; WoD, I'd like if they keep the tone of the different games. the horrific elements just as the, yes, urban fantasy elemnts. The sum of these made the WoD succesfull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T01:13:19-08:00","id":840483,"title":"","content":"My style is epic horror, the background is dark, but only to help to emphasize the light of faith and hope by the heroes. When I create my own stories, I don't mind the official canon at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 03-02-2016, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:42:28-08:00","id":841067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=839820#post839820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see disdain, he's saying that he believes that the World of Darkness' unique element among modern supernatural settings is that it was horror rather than urban fantasy. Now, you can argue that premise (genre definitions are tricky things and the lines are often blurry), but I think it is unfair to read into it that he's putting down urban fantasy. A good parallel, for me, is folks who don't like the new Sherlock Holmes movies because they are action films. This doesn't necessarily mean that they hate action films, just that they don't think the tone fits those particular stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read into what? This is exactly what he said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Where did White Wolf \u201cget it wrong\u201d last time around? What are your least favorite parts of the IP?</b><br /> <br /> Anything that smells of Fantasy. The attempt to create a deep mythology by linking the setting to Exalted was the worst choice ever. That was the last step in WoD\u2019d death-march from being an artistic horror-IP to full on immature, escapist Urban Fantasy. </div> </div> </div>How exactly is that phrase, &quot;immature, escapist Urban Fantasy&quot; supposed to come across as anything but disdain for the genre?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:01:42-08:00","id":841074,"title":"","content":"I just hope we'll get some more books in the next three months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:36:39-08:00","id":841091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf#post830298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">imagonem.org/2016/02/15/white-wolfs-lead-storyteller-there-will-be-a-release-in-2016/<br /> <br /> I really, really don't like the look of things here; the overly edgy tone, the statement that roleplaying games don't sell and that they'll focus almost entirely on videogames, the insistence that pushing the envelope and doing things like working 9/11 into the fluff are good... this just smacks of a shallow corporate buyout by people who don't have a fucking clue. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I respectfully disagree!<br /> <br /> I think the Classic World of Darkness never shied away from making real world events part of their canon, and writting 9/11 in just shows that the writers are aware they shouldn't use two measures to judge the same thing. If its okay to write about rape camps in the Balkans, then it should be okay to write about 9/11. It is fiction, and it is, like comedy, something that should help us cope and metabolize bad things. I think that, in particular, is more than okay in my book!<br /> <br /> But I just draw pictures. I am not a writer. X)<br /> <br /> As for the tabletop side... it is an unfortunate thing that they are not focusing on it, but the fact is that it is a harsh industry! OP works its magic, but it is NO walk in the park by any means! Its for the few, very competent professionals, and what Paradox does best is gaming.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:35:40-08:00","id":841116,"title":"","content":"I mean we already had two editions of urban fantasy with greater (2nd) and lesser (Revised) tinges of utter absurdity and with a subtext of horror whose execution tended to vary dramatically between player groups and supplements. Why not go for an edition that actually embraces the morbidity inherent in premises like Vampire and Wraith (really not sure how this works for Mage unless you spin lovecraftian madness into the magic- for Werewolf I guess you just amp up the Werewolf-on-human brutality and the apocalyptic desperation?)? It's not like all copies of V20 etc. will suddenly vaporize on publication of a new edition- I'd rather have them go too far* into black-and-black morality than a regurgitation of the more of the same. At the very least we'll get the extreme opposite end to 2e's zany madness and will thus have the perfect toolset for hybridizing an actually workable setting (please don't tell me anyone uses the lore raw). <br /> <br /> *It helps that there's no such thing as too GRIMDARK in my book, admittedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 03-03-2016, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:54:52-08:00","id":841125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841116#post841116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean we already had two editions of urban fantasy with greater (2nd) and lesser (Revised) tinges of utter absurdity and with a subtext of horror whose execution tended to vary dramatically between player groups and supplements. Why not go for an edition that actually embraces the morbidity inherent in premises like Vampire and Wraith (really not sure how this works for Mage unless you spin lovecraftian madness into the magic- for Werewolf I guess you just amp up the Werewolf-on-human brutality and the apocalyptic desperation?)? It's not like all copies of V20 etc. will suddenly vaporize on publication of a new edition- I'd rather have them go too far* into black-and-black morality than a regurgitation of the more of the same. At the very least we'll get the extreme opposite end to 2e's zany madness and will thus have the perfect toolset for hybridizing an actually workable setting (please don't tell me anyone uses the lore raw).<br /> <br /> *It helps that there's no such thing as too GRIMDARK in my book, admittedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pushing the grimdark too far wraps around into utter absurdity. Just look at WH 40K for a litany of examples in that vein, and probably Paranoia as well.. &quot;Urban fantasy&quot; elements tend to temper the grimdark so that it actually has a calm moment to catch you off guard before bad shit happens again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:46:38-08:00","id":841173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841116#post841116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean we already had two editions of urban fantasy with greater (2nd) and lesser (Revised) tinges of utter absurdity and with a subtext of horror whose execution tended to vary dramatically between player groups and supplements. Why not go for an edition that actually embraces the morbidity inherent in premises like Vampire and Wraith (really not sure how this works for Mage unless you spin lovecraftian madness into the magic- for Werewolf I guess you just amp up the Werewolf-on-human brutality and the apocalyptic desperation?)? It's not like all copies of V20 etc. will suddenly vaporize on publication of a new edition- I'd rather have them go too far* into black-and-black morality than a regurgitation of the more of the same. At the very least we'll get the extreme opposite end to 2e's zany madness and will thus have the perfect toolset for hybridizing an actually workable setting (please don't tell me anyone uses the lore raw).<br /> <br /> *It helps that there's no such thing as too GRIMDARK in my book, admittedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that GRIMDARK is a bad thing? It's an absurd joke, and not an actual positive. Also, you're paining the games there with a very broad brush. Werewolf and Mage do not need any darkening. They have been different games from the start, one not really giving a fuck, and the other being dark and messed up in a whole different way.<br /> <br /> As for Wraith... Not sure if you are serious, but that game is probably one of the bleakest and moodiest things ever written. I find the books hard to read, and the ideas within deeply disturbing. It makes for a brilliant setting and a great game, but it's already not for every group and every game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:51:50-08:00","id":841175,"title":"","content":"When you say grim dark world of darkness all I see is skulls and pauldrons on everything. Can Cain be the god emperor of vampire kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T05:41:12-08:00","id":841239,"title":"","content":"In the Grim Darkness of the 2nd millennium, there is only Humanity loss.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I don't really care what WW does as long as the X20 PoDs are available long enough for me to finish university, get a job, and buy them. Heck, I see little reason not to leave the PoDs available for eternity, unless there's some fee for doing so that I don't know about. (Yes, even V20, I don't have the money for a copy right now)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:41:54-08:00","id":841353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You do realise that GRIMDARK is a bad thing? It's an absurd joke, </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean, unless you're someone like me who revels in utter unrelenting bleakness. Honestly while I much enjoyed the parts of 40k that weren't Space Marines, it really hasn't even been consistently all that exaggeratedly dark for the past while anyway (insofar as GW's more often than not bad writing has ever been consistent). It certainly could've gone a few notches higher!<br /> <br /> Considering the soaring heights of monstrosity that especially brutalized (the Mongol, Timurid, and related steppe-raider conquests) or especially insane (Hitler &amp; friends, Stalin &amp; friends, Pol Pot &amp; friends, etc.) elements of humanity have achieved (often well beyond what most fiction authors can apparently conceive of), WoD has tended to be pretty tame. I mean, I distinctly remember the Midnight Siege supplement being from an authorial perspective (and in reference to the reactions of some younger Kindred) aghast at the notion of certain elders backing racist politics because the Sabbat was proportionately more Hispanic or something- as if in a society of immortal undead monsters who routinely eat and enslave people locked in a war for survival against apocalyptic madmen, moderate institutional racism (traffic stops etc.) within their prey population would even register as noteworthy on the collective moral radar much less be something that was *stressed* as unsavory (....compared to all the usual murder and exploitation). Given the routine neglect for even basic concerns of the Humanity downward spiral shown in many elements of the backstory (full Sabbat Black Hand agents at Humanity 5?) not to mention among player groups, I'd certainly say that WoD badly needed polishing on that front.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't exactly call WtA as written all that &quot;dark&quot;. I mean yeah it had nice fatalistic apocalyptic themes but Pentex was an amalgam of Captain Planet villains often goofily conflating whatever the authors personally disliked (frat culture etc.) with cosmic evil while manufacturing bane-infused cereal or whatever nonsense. They even ruined the pathos and bleakness of the fomori by having them be mostly mass-produced evil minions for Pentex (rather than the gut-wrenching outcome of a life derailed into despair or hatred as in the Freak Legion intro comic). One of the major villains basically couldn't be taken seriously at all and routinely trashed the atmosphere whenever it showed up in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 03-03-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T11:35:52-08:00","id":841405,"title":"","content":"If I am sincere, I want to buy Wraith20 not to play &quot;lords of the tears in the empire of the sadness&quot; but something like &quot;Ghostbusters vs Beetlejuice&quot;, the videogame &quot;Dante's Inferno&quot;, Grimm Fandango or &quot;Murdered: soul suspect&quot;, &quot;Painkiller&quot; or or like the comic &quot;Requiem knight vampire&quot;, or to be used like allies (or nemesis) of another PCs from another lines, for example the mummies and the kue-jins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:29:17-08:00","id":841565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841353#post841353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I mean, unless you're someone like me who revels in utter unrelenting bleakness. Honestly while I much enjoyed the parts of 40k that weren't Space Marines, it really hasn't even been consistently all that exaggeratedly dark for the past while anyway (insofar as GW's more often than not bad writing has ever been consistent). It certainly could've gone a few notches higher!<br /> <br /> Considering the soaring heights of monstrosity that especially brutalized (the Mongol, Timurid, and related steppe-raider conquests) or especially insane (Hitler &amp; friends, Stalin &amp; friends, Pol Pot &amp; friends, etc.) elements of humanity have achieved (often well beyond what most fiction authors can apparently conceive of), WoD has tended to be pretty tame. I mean, I distinctly remember the Midnight Siege supplement being from an authorial perspective (and in reference to the reactions of some younger Kindred) aghast at the notion of certain elders backing racist politics because the Sabbat was proportionately more Hispanic or something- as if in a society of immortal undead monsters who routinely eat and enslave people locked in a war for survival against apocalyptic madmen, moderate institutional racism (traffic stops etc.) within their prey population would even register as noteworthy on the collective moral radar much less be something that was *stressed* as unsavory (....compared to all the usual murder and exploitation). Given the routine neglect for even basic concerns of the Humanity downward spiral shown in many elements of the backstory (full Sabbat Black Hand agents at Humanity 5?) not to mention among player groups, I'd certainly say that WoD badly needed polishing on that front.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't exactly call WtA as written all that &quot;dark&quot;. I mean yeah it had nice fatalistic apocalyptic themes but Pentex was an amalgam of Captain Planet villains</div> </div> </div> </div>Empty reference is empty and misses the target. If you want to see anything that actually had points in common with Captain Planet, go to Mage. On the other hand, the details on Pentex from the BotW 2nd edition on reads more like The Devil's Advocate. &quot;What did I say? Vanity!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> often goofily conflating whatever the authors personally disliked (frat culture etc.) with cosmic evil while manufacturing bane-infused cereal or whatever nonsense. They even ruined the pathos and bleakness of the fomori by having them be mostly mass-produced evil minions for Pentex (rather than the gut-wrenching outcome of a life derailed into despair or hatred as in the Freak Legion intro comic). One of the major villains basically couldn't be taken seriously at all and routinely trashed the atmosphere whenever it showed up in the background. </div> </div> </div>Bane-infused anything got retconned out in W20, following a late 2nd edition and on into Revised push to keep it out of the game. Banes don't need to be infused into anything; they're already all around in most urban environments. King Distilleries doesn't produce fomori from tainted drinks' it just gets people to drink their life away on normal booze, which has terrible sides of its own, as shown by real world consequences of said actions. The horror in W:tA is that everday, normal living is bad for the world, and yet, also so pervasively baked into carrying on that trying to stop it is basically something you can only faintly imagine and wish for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:39:36-08:00","id":841572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841353#post841353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I mean, unless you're someone like me who revels in utter unrelenting bleakness. Honestly while I much enjoyed the parts of 40k that weren't Space Marines, it really hasn't even been consistently all that exaggeratedly dark for the past while anyway (insofar as GW's more often than not bad writing has ever been consistent). It certainly could've gone a few notches higher!<br /> <br /> Considering the soaring heights of monstrosity that especially brutalized (the Mongol, Timurid, and related steppe-raider conquests) or especially insane (Hitler &amp; friends, Stalin &amp; friends, Pol Pot &amp; friends, etc.) elements of humanity have achieved (often well beyond what most fiction authors can apparently conceive of), WoD has tended to be pretty tame. I mean, I distinctly remember the Midnight Siege supplement being from an authorial perspective (and in reference to the reactions of some younger Kindred) aghast at the notion of certain elders backing racist politics because the Sabbat was proportionately more Hispanic or something- as if in a society of immortal undead monsters who routinely eat and enslave people locked in a war for survival against apocalyptic madmen, moderate institutional racism (traffic stops etc.) within their prey population would even register as noteworthy on the collective moral radar much less be something that was *stressed* as unsavory (....compared to all the usual murder and exploitation). Given the routine neglect for even basic concerns of the Humanity downward spiral shown in many elements of the backstory (full Sabbat Black Hand agents at Humanity 5?) not to mention among player groups, I'd certainly say that WoD badly needed polishing on that front.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't exactly call WtA as written all that &quot;dark&quot;. I mean yeah it had nice fatalistic apocalyptic themes but Pentex was an amalgam of Captain Planet villains often goofily conflating whatever the authors personally disliked (frat culture etc.) with cosmic evil while manufacturing bane-infused cereal or whatever nonsense. They even ruined the pathos and bleakness of the fomori by having them be mostly mass-produced evil minions for Pentex (rather than the gut-wrenching outcome of a life derailed into despair or hatred as in the Freak Legion intro comic). One of the major villains basically couldn't be taken seriously at all and routinely trashed the atmosphere whenever it showed up in the background.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think grimdark means what you think it means. Historically accurate attrocity and people being bastards to each other is par of course for the World of Darkness. Black on black for sake of blackness and edgyness is not.<br /> <br /> As for Werewolf, it's a very shallow reading you're showing there. I'd look deeper for the actual darkness within. It's insidious, maddening and deeply disturbing. Your referring to Freak Legion rather then Possesed is rather indicative.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:41:21-08:00","id":841573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841405#post841405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am sincere, I want to buy Wraith20 not to play &quot;lords of the tears in the empire of the sadness&quot; but something like &quot;Ghostbusters vs Beetlejuice&quot;, the videogame &quot;Dante's Inferno&quot;, Grimm Fandango or &quot;Murdered: soul suspect&quot;, &quot;Painkiller&quot; or or like the comic &quot;Requiem knight vampire&quot;, or to be used like allies (or nemesis) of another PCs from another lines, for example the mummies and the kue-jins.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's gonna take your books away if that's what you want to do, but that's not what Wraith is about. The pathos, shadow and the erosion of fetters ensure a very different tone for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:17:19-08:00","id":841776,"title":"","content":"I mean when I buy the books after I create my own version of WoD. Like a building toys I create what I want, and it hasn't to be like you seen in the box. If I don't like the canon background, I destroy it and I use my own mash-up. You can create a &quot;Wraith&quot; where the afterlife is like Stephen King's &quot;Revival&quot; and I can create my own version of revival where the R.I.P.D kick-ass the &quot;Mother&quot; and can travel to the lands of the dreams where they aren't wellcome by the lord faes.<br /> <br /> I only use the parts (powers, factions) I like. If I want, I forget the storytelling system and I use my own version of d20 Modern.<br /> <br /> If I can mix Changeling the Dreaming and Changeling the lost I do it because I have fun, I enjoy doing different things it is my game with my imagination. I haven't to be loyal to the canon background. That would be like the glue in the LEGO movie.<br /> <br /> * In my stories I can add surprises, for example a little squad of vampires of Sabbath are hunting and the target is a poor single mother and her child... to allow her daughter to run away she sacrifice herself.... and the vampires discover after the mother's death her blood is become a poisonous &quot;venom&quot;, because she is like a martyr, she died to save her daughter (and now her body and blood it is like a sacred relic and holy water). It isn't canon at allo, but it's my story and then I allow it to be possible,<br /> <br /> * About controversy stories linked to the real world, please, don't forget the respect to human dignity and understanding for the people who is suffering. Have you thought about controversy because a stupy one did anything wrong? For example a fanboy who watched &quot;V of the Vendetta&quot; and after created a bomb, or black metal fans burnings churchs like Norway in the 90's years.<br /> <br /> I am sure you don't want a new anti-rpg version of Fredric Wertham's &quot;Seduction of the Innocent&quot; by fault somebody published something and later a stupy does something horrible. (I am not kidding, a nail bomb in a Catholic cathedral isn't ficiont, it happened in Spain, in Almudena, but it didn't explode and nobody was hurt).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 03-04-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:54:07-08:00","id":841789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841776#post841776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* About controversy stories linked to the real world, please, don't forget the respect to human dignity and understanding for the people who is suffering. Have you thought about controversy because a stupy one did anything wrong? For example a fanboy who watched &quot;V of the Vendetta&quot; and after created a bomb, or black metal fans burnings churchs like Norway in the 90's years.<br /> <br /> I am sure you don't want a new anti-rpg version of Fredric Wertham's &quot;Seduction of the Innocent&quot; by fault somebody published something and later a stupy does something horrible. (I am not kidding, a nail bomb in a Catholic cathedral isn't ficiont, it happened in Spain, in Almudena, but it didn't explode and nobody was hurt).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... what. WHAT!? Dude. I know you have issues expressing yourself and have a tendency to flail around with english, but there is no correlation between there being mature material and there being idiots who will do crazy shit. The moral panic is caused by bad parents who cannot take the responsibility for not taking better care of the mental and emotional state of their poor kids.<br /> <br /> Instead of realising that there are disturbed people who need to be taken care of and prevented from breaking, we blame every stupid little thing for why they snapped. Some people are just broken, it's a sad fact. Books, Comics, RPG's, computer games.... they've all been placed as convenient excuses, but at the end of the day, the problem is in deeply disturbed people, not in the material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T06:40:34-08:00","id":841865,"title":"","content":"The fault is by people who don't teach (or have fogorten) to respect the human dignity. White Wolf and the rest of publisher companies should be careful to avoid that moral panic because it is bad for the business.<br /> <br /> * Of course it is only fiction, &quot;Twilight&quot; saga is only books and the most of people from real world don't want to be true vampires... (but to kill Edward Cullen (or Bella Swan)!!!)<br /> <br /> ....but you should realice some things may be annoying for others. For example the comic &quot;Titin in Congo&quot; today is banned in lot of places because it's supposedly racist. You may find people with other point of view about the limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:58:17-08:00","id":842102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=841572#post841572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a very shallow reading you're showing there. I'd look deeper for the actual darkness within. It's insidious, maddening and deeply disturbing. Your referring to Freak Legion rather then Possesed is rather indicative.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness and the games that are a part of it can hold different meanings for different people. There's nothing wrong with holding a different perspective from your own.<br /> <br /> Try to lighten up with the condescending attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:02:51-08:00","id":842139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842102#post842102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The World of Darkness and the games that are a part of it can hold different meanings for different people. There's nothing wrong with holding a different perspective from your own.<br /> <br /> Try to lighten up with the condescending attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, &quot;Werewolf is Captain Planet&quot; is entirely and solely a terrible, outdated shallow reading that needs to die. It's been trotted out time and again over the past two decades even as media that deals with similar subject manner with far different execution have come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-04-2016, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:17:02-08:00","id":842148,"title":"","content":"My opinion is &quot;W:tA&quot; is really a Captain Planet for adults. Garous want mankind to come back to the stone age. It isn't about responsibility for the future generations but technophobie.<br /> <br /> I hate the triad (Kaos, Weaver and Wyrn) because in the real world the order isn't frozen but flexible, and the dynamism to create and to change the things means willpower, hard work and discipline. The creativity also needs self-control. Please, forget that bullshit about &quot;creativity means breaking all the rules&quot;. Please, somebody dislikes me because I like to break the canon background for my campaigns.<br /> <br /> The garous are the closest one to be cartoon characters, Never WoD has been white vs black, without gray zones in the middle, that garous and company againts the wyrn. Never in another part from WoD the (anti-)hero-evil axis has been so clear and manichaeist.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 03-06-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:09:06-08:00","id":842305,"title":"","content":"So what's this thing about someone posting to 4chan claiming to be an author for Paradox' WoD, talking about vampires being explicitly soulless, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T21:32:26-08:00","id":842402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842305#post842305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's this thing about someone posting to 4chan claiming to be an author for Paradox' WoD, talking about vampires being explicitly soulless, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what became of it but I would take that with a skeptical eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:06:17-08:00","id":842477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842305#post842305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's this thing about someone posting to 4chan claiming to be an author for Paradox' WoD, talking about vampires being explicitly soulless, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>It got deleted here. There is no sure evidence that it was David Hill who wrote it, but I guess we will know when the Black Hand book is out if it was bullshit or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:31:07-08:00","id":842494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842402#post842402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what became of it but I would take that with a skeptical eye.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842477#post842477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It got deleted here. There is no sure evidence that it was David Hill who wrote it, but I guess we will know when the Black Hand book is out if it was bullshit or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw the 4chan post so I don't know what all it contained. I totally agree about taking it with a skeptical eye because 4chan, but I was curious about the claims made in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:27:58-08:00","id":842604,"title":"","content":"Basically,someone posting as DavidH claimed the WW used their editorial control of WoD products to insist on the new book having an extremely strong official game stance on a metaphysical issue in VtM that is problematic with a lot of the Black Hand material if turned into the specific objective fact claimed was injected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:56:23-08:00","id":842692,"title":"","content":"May very well not be David Hill who wrote. The guy has some dedicated enemies and I could see them pulling something like that to sabotage things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T15:53:36-08:00","id":842754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842148#post842148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion is &quot;W:tA&quot; is really a Captain Planet for adults. Garous want mankind to come back to the stone age. It isn't about responsibility for the future generations but technophobie.<br /> <br /> I hate the triad (Kaos, Weaver and Wyrn) because in the real world the order isn't frozen but flexible, and the dynamism to create and to change the things means willpower, hardwork and discipline. The creativity also needs self-control. Please, forget that bullshit about &quot;creativity means breaking all the rules&quot;. Please, somebody dislikes me to break the canon background for my campaigns.<br /> <br /> The garous are the closest one to be cartoon characters, Never WoD has been white vs black, without gray zones that garous and company againts the wyrn. Never in another part from WoD the (anti-)hero vs the evil axis has been so clear.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The setup could have been made that simple way back when, but even first edition was more complicated than that, and it hasn't let up, given how the past twenty years have been a steady procession of &quot;the Garou fucked up, the Wyld isn't your friend or anyone else's, and you'll probably end up fighting the people that you shouldn't because they have a very justified grudge against you.&quot; And actually doing what's going to get you out of that shitty situation? It could very well cost you your standing among your own, and leave you high and dry. Renown for Garou is calibrated for upholding Garou cultural values, after all, and reconciling with the Fera will usually go against it because of how much territory and how many treasured relics you'll have to give up. The withdrawl from the Amazon only happened because most of the Garou actually had home septs and came from a long way away; doing that on home territory and getting rid of older fetishes is not going to happen without much arm-twisting and many enemies made among your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:37:54-08:00","id":842771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842604#post842604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically,someone posting as DavidH claimed the WW used their editorial control of WoD products to insist on the new book having an extremely strong official game stance on a metaphysical issue in VtM that is problematic with a lot of the Black Hand material if turned into the specific objective fact claimed was injected.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842692#post842692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May very well not be David Hill who wrote. The guy has some dedicated enemies and I could see them pulling something like that to sabotage things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, both of you. That clarifies it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I totally agree with the skepticism but I didn't know the whole story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:40:33-08:00","id":842774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842692#post842692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May very well not be David Hill who wrote. The guy has some dedicated enemies and I could see them pulling something like that to sabotage things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just adorable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:54:20-08:00","id":842786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842754#post842754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setup could have been made that simple way back when, but even first edition was more complicated than that, and it hasn't let up, given how the past twenty years have been a steady procession of &quot;the Garou fucked up, the Wyld isn't your friend or anyone else's, and you'll probably end up fighting the people that you shouldn't because they have a very justified grudge against you.&quot; And actually doing what's going to get you out of that shitty situation? It could very well cost you your standing among your own, and leave you high and dry. Renown for Garou is calibrated for upholding Garou cultural values, after all, and reconciling with the Fera will usually go against it because of how much territory and how many treasured relics you'll have to give up. The withdrawl from the Amazon only happened because most of the Garou actually had home septs and came from a long way away; doing that on home territory and getting rid of older fetishes is not going to happen without much arm-twisting and many enemies made among your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, most people get their info on Werewolf from either a shallow reading or from secondhand spiel on the internet. Like all that stuff how it's all about combat, or how it's all about captain planet. Yet if someone actually sat down and read just the core books from one end to the other, I have no idea how they could claim the same claptrap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T09:44:36-08:00","id":843022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=842786#post842786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, most people get their info on Werewolf from either a shallow reading or from secondhand spiel on the internet. Like all that stuff how it's all about combat, or how it's all about captain planet. Yet if someone actually sat down and read just the core books from one end to the other, I have no idea how they could claim the same claptrap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have sat down and read the core book in several editions plus numerous, numerous supplements and I can <i>easily </i>see how people could claim &quot;the same claptrap&quot;. Not only are those things painted all over the game, many, many, many people play Werewolf EXACTLY that way. To which, I could add some serious reductionist animistic &quot;kumbaya&quot; mutualistic, self-reinforcing solipsism.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Werewolf isn't anything else, nor that it was even meant to be more than that (or, at the very least, to handle the flip side of each of those things in a dynamic game setting... whether they entirely succeeded or not is up for debate). That doesn't mean it has it's own coolness for the values of coolness that it embodies but it doesn't mean that the criticisms of it aren't warranted. Particularly when Werewolf partisans can be particularly strident in slopping Werewolf's core mythology as the &quot;One True Way of which all others are pale and mistaken imitations and reflections&quot;.<br /> <br /> My central complaint with Werewolf is how, unlike the other games (excluding Hunter for obvious reasons), it doesn't really even give a passing nod to the concepts of &quot;werewolf-dom&quot; that existed before the game. It gives a failed attempt at a gloss that is completely washed out by it's own conceptualizations. Without substantive changes you still can't even play many/most of the werewolf-genre stories within the context of the game.<br /> <br /> However, all that being said, it looks like the next iteration of Werewolf that is coming isn't going to address any of these concerns. And why would it? After all those things are already on a spectrum of &quot;acceptable&quot; to &quot;what we play for&quot;. But it looks like it might dial up other aspects by several notches. I have the feeling that the whole &quot;struggle against impossible odds&quot; will skew past &quot;let's alt least go down fighting&quot; all the way to &quot;we haven't committed suicide yet because we are too weak to admit it that we are just shit, so we lash out at everyone and everything&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-06-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T16:18:29-08:00","id":843175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843022#post843022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have sat down and read the core book in several editions plus numerous, numerous supplements and I can <i>easily </i>see how people could claim &quot;the same claptrap&quot;. Not only are those things painted all over the game, many, many, many people play Werewolf EXACTLY that way. To which, I could add some serious reductionist animistic &quot;kumbaya&quot; mutualistic, self-reinforcing solipsism.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Werewolf isn't anything else, nor that it was even meant to be more than that (or, at the very least, to handle the flip side of each of those things in a dynamic game setting... whether they entirely succeeded or not is up for debate). That doesn't mean it has it's own coolness for the values of coolness that it embodies but it doesn't mean that the criticisms of it aren't warranted. Particularly when Werewolf partisans can be particularly strident in slopping Werewolf's core mythology as the &quot;One True Way of which all others are pale and mistaken imitations and reflections&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is about the same attitude presented by Mage partisans who insist on the Consensus, Vampire partisans insisting on God and Caine, Demon partisans insisting on everyone being clueless but them and so on. All of them are wrong because they should learn to respect the other games. Just like people should learn to enjoy the games thesmelves on their own merits. What's your point?<br /> <br /> As far as core values of Werewolf... I find the whole sentiment rather off kilter, since the enemy is not Captain Planet and the Triat is anything but simple and straighforward. The one thing that the game does is give you a just cause to fight for, which I would argue Mage does as well not making the game stand out. The message of the game is not even about environment per se as it's a critique of the human condition, and how humans being assholes to each other feed other things that make the world worse and reinforce all the evils that we do. The only valid response to such a crapsack world are monsters willing to push them back. Yet the monsters themselves have a very hard time not being human. So, no I do not see anything simple, straightforward or black and white. You are a holy warrior with a cause, but that does not mean that the world you live in supports your narrative or that you can actually live with yourself (considering what rage does to you, you're shit out of luck finding companions that are not utter bastions of patience).<br /> <br /> Add to this the rich culture, history, religion and of the Garou, the motley crew and additional complications of the Fera, the clever interplay of mythology and the setting... and you actually have a pretty nice game that stands well on its own two feet. So yeah, I don't see where anyone can get twocolor simplicity or captain planet.<br /> <br /> Captain Planet is about a guy who cannot punch a person and hippie 90s kids fighting ridiculous villians who seeek profit in random acts of polution.<br /> Werewolf is about religious terrorists murdering humans and the monsters hiding among them in their holy war to save humanity from themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843022#post843022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My central complaint with Werewolf is how, unlike the other games (excluding Hunter for obvious reasons), it doesn't really even give a passing nod to the concepts of &quot;werewolf-dom&quot; that existed before the game. It gives a failed attempt at a gloss that is completely washed out by it's own conceptualizations. Without substantive changes you still can't even play many/most of the werewolf-genre stories within the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how much postmodernist solipstistic philosophical manifestos have with witchcraft and religon, or how much Vampire The Masquerade has with actual mythological vampires, I have very little issues with Werewolves being defined by being shapeshifters and then spinning off into something else. I've heard a lot of complaints about this, but I really don't see why it's so hard to take Werewolf at its own merits. Mind you, it might not be your cup of tea, but stop slagging it off and let people have their own fun*<br /> <br /> * Not you personaly, but this is a statement meant for everyone who just shits all over Werewolf without even bothering to actually figure out what it's about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T20:03:38-08:00","id":843262,"title":"","content":"To me it sounds like Paradox will handle things pretty well and even I realize that computer games do better in this age than TT games does. I think that its better that they focus on a media that is profitable and will reach a greater audience, with TT as a side product, than put all the money on a media that isn't at its top any more. Video games will should create interest and money for the World of Darkness in a way that a TT game simply can't, to my knowledge, do today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T01:37:02-08:00","id":843320,"title":"","content":"As someone who has been to other Werewolf forums/sites in the past outside of White Wolf/Onyx Path itself, and I mean places that discuss werewolves and not W:tA:<br /> I will always find this reasoning deeply ironic and just shake my head at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843022#post843022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Particularly when Werewolf partisans can be particularly strident in slopping Werewolf's core mythology as the &quot;One True Way of which all others are pale and mistaken imitations and reflections</b></i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> My central complaint with Werewolf is how, unlike the other games (excluding Hunter for obvious reasons), <i><b>it doesn't really even give a passing nod to the concepts of &quot;werewolf-dom&quot;</b> </i>that existed before the game. It gives a failed attempt at a gloss that is completely washed out by it's own conceptualizations. Without substantive changes you still can't even play many/most of the werewolf-genre stories within the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen both Werewolf and Therianthrope communities commit to their own versions of the &quot;No True Werewolf&quot; fallacy (<i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_true_Scotsman\" target=\"_blank\">This is a variation of the &quot;No True Scotsman&quot; fallacy</a></i>).<br /> The people behind the Werewolf Horror Calendar even had a statement about it being against &quot;Hippie Wolves&quot;, &quot;Regular Wolves&quot;, and &quot;Twilight Beefcake Wolves&quot;. Werewolf-News.com even joined in when promoting the calendar.<br /> And yes, Werewolf: the Apocalypse is often derided as being part of the &quot;Hippie Wolves&quot; or &quot;New Age Wolves&quot; segment that Werewolf fans hate.<br /> <i><b>So a lot of these people practice the very same thing you are claiming W:tA fans do. Sometimes without realizing it.</b></i><br /> <br /> I get really tired when the &quot;W:tA doesn't stay close to actual Werewolf myths and folklore!&quot; always gets brought up. Especially when some werewolf fans cite Werewolf movies as the actual myth/lore without much deeper insight into where certain ideas actually came from and that some of these ideas have no real connections (<i>Silver, being bitten, etc.</i>).<br /> So what you are really talking about is that modern media werewolf-genre mainly influenced by Universal's The Wolf Man from the 1940's is taken as the true &quot;lore&quot; and usually outright ignoring a huge swath of much older stories about how varied werewolves can actually be.<br /> <br /> Even the whole &quot;Werewolf's bite infection&quot; is suspect and cited as being a more modern idea that had hardly has any basis in the old lore.<br /> And yet some Werewolf movie influenced fans get so unhappy whenever something doesn't have the &quot;bite&quot; in it.<br /> These same type of fans were quick to support Forsaken when it came out, but quickly jumped ship on Forsaken as well when it didn't hold up to their other impossible standards of what &quot;werewolf-dom&quot; should be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Getting back on topic:</b></u><br /> I wonder if Paradox will break the W:tA video/computer game curse?<br /> There was Capcom's Season of the Wolf for the PS1/Saturn that didn't come to pass once Capcom and White Wolf parted ways. And then there was ASC/Dreamforge's Heart of Gaia for the PC that became vaporware.<br /> <br /> Looking through old Inquest magazines, I guess there was news going around at the time that some company was trying to make a Mage computer game as well and yet nothing came out of it.<br /> <br /> I also wonder if Paradox managed to get any rights to the Rage CCG, Arcadia CCG, or V:tES. Would love to see a Print on Demand versions or apps/games in the style of the Yu-gi-oh Tag Force games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T04:11:40-08:00","id":843354,"title":"","content":"Today the most famous werewolves aren't the garous, or Jacob Black from Twightlight books, but the main characters from teleserie &quot;Teen Wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> To create my own stories I don't respect the canon background at all, for example I allow skin dancers who only need to kill five fomorians, not five garous, to become a werewolf, Or a new race of werewolves like formorian gameplay traits, but wolf spirits instead banes.<br /> <br /> My opinion is WoD videogames would need a new setting because storytelling system isn't easy to be adapted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:10:41-08:00","id":843409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843354#post843354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today the most famous werewolves aren't the garous, or Jacob Black from Twightlight books, but the main characters from teleserie &quot;Teen Wolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only matters for how you're determining presentation..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To create my own stories I don't respect the canon background at all, for example I allow skin dancers who only need to kill five fomorians, not five garous, to become a werewolf, Or a new race of werewolves like formorian gameplay traits, but wolf spirits instead banes<br /> <br /> My opinion is WoD videogames would need a new setting because storytelling system isn't easy to be adapted. </div> </div> </div>You're talking about two different things, there. The setting isn't the system, though the system has a few things to try and help with some touchpoints, like Rage and Gnosis. And the adjustments that the setting could use don't necessarily fall in line with what you're suggesting; mostly, they involve details like stronger setups for characters no longer in their early teens and name changes for a certain breed of character for the Garou and the Fera that have the same equivalent (the Nagah being an obvious exception on account of having their equivalent being named &quot;ahi&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T08:01:02-08:00","id":843441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843320#post843320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder if Paradox managed to get any rights to the Rage CCG, Arcadia CCG, or V:tES. Would love to see a Print on Demand versions or apps/games in the style of the Yu-gi-oh Tag Force games.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have expressed a strong interest in bringing back V:tES in some form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T08:58:05-08:00","id":843459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843354#post843354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today the most famous werewolves aren't the garous, or Jacob Black from Twightlight books, but the main characters from teleserie &quot;Teen Wolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, aren't Garou the same kind of werewolves that we see in Twilight and Teenwolf? They are hereditary werewolves who aren't contagious. They can generally control their transformations. Pretty similar considering the wide range of different depictions of werewolves out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:18:04-08:00","id":843473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843459#post843459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, aren't Garou the same kind of werewolves that we see in Twilight and Teenwolf? They are hereditary werewolves who aren't contagious. They can generally control their transformations. Pretty similar considering the wide range of different depictions of werewolves out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a hereditary werewolf is definitely NOT something new, so that's one of the few places the WtA synced up. However, being a hereditary werewolf instead of an infected werewolf isn't really the defining trait of WtA at all, is it? Teen Wolf and Twilight aren't focused on animistic killing machines trying to defend Planet Earth from (mostly human) corruption.<br /> <br /> Sure you COULD play a Teen Wolf inspired game, but you will be minimizing or chucking significant chunks of the game. You could probably accomplish the same slightly better with WtF but still there's a lot that doesn't fit at all. <br /> <br /> Also, WtA was published in 1992, Teen Wolf became a TV series in 2011 and the Twilight series stated in 2004. If there was any influence (not much, since the premise you stated isn't an invention of WtA) it would have to be the other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:31:46-08:00","id":843482,"title":"","content":"Calm down, I wasn't claiming that W:tA was based on Twilight or Teenwolf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just that they are similar in having heredity werewolves. Which I'm not saying is new either, though when you go back before Hollywood werewolves in the early 20th century, there aren't that many consistent werewolf or shape shifter legends anyway, I mean the old myths are all over the place.<br /> <br /> Though, Teenwolf the movie predates W:tA by quite some time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:45:10-08:00","id":843490,"title":"","content":"Some players don't play the background of WoD rpgs but they use the storytelling system (and powers) to roleplay their favorite franchises, for example &quot;Underworld&quot; movies or &quot;True Blood&quot; books/teleserie. Some storytellers or Game Masters would rather to &quot;borrow&quot; ideas from another sources to surprise players who have readen all metaplot from internet....or because reading wikis from books, movies, videogames and teleseries is cheaper than buying books about background.<br /> <br /> Internet and videogames changed rpg industry. <br /> <br /> * My own version of the &quot;cursed werewolf&quot; is like the main character from the manga &quot;crying freeman&quot;, a man with the spirit of dragon within, forced to be a hitman. For game mechanic effects, it would by like a furry version of fomoris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:50:43-08:00","id":843495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843175#post843175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is about the same attitude presented by Mage partisans who insist on the Consensus, Vampire partisans insisting on God and Caine, Demon partisans insisting on everyone being clueless but them and so on. All of them are wrong because they should learn to respect the other games. Just like people should learn to enjoy the games thesmelves on their own merits. What's your point?<br /> <br /> As far as core values of Werewolf... I find the whole sentiment rather off kilter, since the enemy is not Captain Planet and the Triat is anything but simple and straighforward. The one thing that the game does is give you a just cause to fight for, which I would argue Mage does as well not making the game stand out. The message of the game is not even about environment per se as it's a critique of the human condition, and how humans being assholes to each other feed other things that make the world worse and reinforce all the evils that we do. The only valid response to such a crapsack world are monsters willing to push them back. Yet the monsters themselves have a very hard time not being human. So, no I do not see anything simple, straightforward or black and white. You are a holy warrior with a cause, but that does not mean that the world you live in supports your narrative or that you can actually live with yourself (considering what rage does to you, you're shit out of luck finding companions that are not utter bastions of patience).<br /> <br /> Add to this the rich culture, history, religion and of the Garou, the motley crew and additional complications of the Fera, the clever interplay of mythology and the setting... and you actually have a pretty nice game that stands well on its own two feet. So yeah, I don't see where anyone can get twocolor simplicity or captain planet.<br /> <br /> Captain Planet is about a guy who cannot punch a person and hippie 90s kids fighting ridiculous villians who seeek profit in random acts of polution.<br /> Werewolf is about religious terrorists murdering humans and the monsters hiding among them in their holy war to save humanity from themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Considering how much postmodernist solipstistic philosophical manifestos have with witchcraft and religon, or how much Vampire The Masquerade has with actual mythological vampires, I have very little issues with Werewolves being defined by being shapeshifters and then spinning off into something else. I've heard a lot of complaints about this, but I really don't see why it's so hard to take Werewolf at its own merits. Mind you, it might not be your cup of tea, but stop slagging it off and let people have their own fun*<br /> <br /> * Not you personaly, but this is a statement meant for everyone who just shits all over Werewolf without even bothering to actually figure out what it's about.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is more that people who see WtA that way and DON'T shit on it, but take it at that level and enjoy the hell out of it or decide it isn't for them, are not being the kind of assholes you are railing against. It's specious to say that WtA isn't all those things, because it is. AND it is something more as well, if you dig in deeper. What you've described and several other things as well (fetish hunting can definitely give a D&amp;D dungeon spelunker vibe). Hell, my favorite all-time WtA experience was a semi-LARP real-time political in-fighting thriller at Gen Con. And the politics was was as deep and nasty as I've seen in VtM (which is suppose to be &quot;that&quot; game.... or was. Not sure under the new vision. Politics would only seem relevant in how oppressive it was and how it increased the suicidal inner urges of young Kindred in making their lives even darker and more bleak and hopeless. When we had finished up our last game, I put a WtA mini-chronicle on the table as one of the options for our next foray, after having included significant Werewolf elements in last mini-chronicle. <br /> <br /> But I DO understand some of the integral reasoning. At the first look, making Werewolves infection driven 1) makes it seems like a Vampire clone when VtM was the only other kid on the block &amp; 2) it causes a whole host of problems of it's own (the x-risk factor is hard to ignore.... werewolves aren't limited by trying to keep a human herd around as blood sheep, what limits would there be on their spread.) They needed to make Werewolf DIFFERENT and the eco-terrorist thing was definitely a way to go (perhaps even an inspired one). It made sense to picking option B (hereditary werewolves) out instead of A (infection-driver), C (both) or D (other ways from mythology, like skin-changers, cursed by God, etc.). I WILL question the primacy of the Umbra and spirits. That is just an odd add on. It's like someone LOVED the Tremere and just wanted every werewolf to be dripping with magic. But, whatever. It was a weird choice, but, apparently, it WORKED for the values of worked that they wanted. <br /> <br /> Onto a matter of relevance to the OP of the thread. Your statement about the various partisanship cabals is well-taken. However, what happens to the games involved if those concerns are all resolved by Paradox? How would people feel about playing a Vampire game where the whole Caine thing is actually part of the tale of the Triat? Or Werewlf players about finding out that the Triat was actually a misunderstood tidbit from the Caine mythology? Many Mage players complain that they feel the Triat is forced on Mage's core mythology like a straight-jacket two sizes too small, so how would they feel when that became canon? Or, vice versa, if everyone else found out that their mythologies were just some kind of Reality Zone under the aegis of Mage's Tellurian? Because those are genuine concerns with a stated goal of ONE World of Darkness. It seems like a &quot;Grand Reconciliation&quot; would be in order, and I'm not sure who is going to be happy with that.... (Except for the partisans of the line that gets &quot;mythological precedence&quot;, which sounds like it's probably going to be Vampire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T12:26:00-08:00","id":843557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843495#post843495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I WILL question the primacy of the Umbra and spirits. That is just an odd add on. It's like someone LOVED the Tremere and just wanted every werewolf to be dripping with magic. But, whatever. It was a weird choice, but, apparently, it WORKED for the values of worked that they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that it had little to nothing to do with the Tremere. Rather, various causes for the existence of werewolves and other beast shapeshifters were attributed to totemic guardians, spiritual possession, or being bridges between this world and the next or another one, given association with shamanic practice in pre-Hollywood sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T15:45:43-08:00","id":843647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843557#post843557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that it had little to nothing to do with the Tremere. Rather, various causes for the existence of werewolves and other beast shapeshifters were attributed to totemic guardians, spiritual possession, or being bridges between this world and the next or another one, given association with shamanic practice in pre-Hollywood sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to this that Werewolf wanted to be honestly spiritual. Not the Post-Modernist New Age spiritualism of Mage, but honest to God Faith and Religion with actual consequences and problems it introduces to the people that have to face its impact on the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843495#post843495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onto a matter of relevance to the OP of the thread. Your statement about the various partisanship cabals is well-taken. However, what happens to the games involved if those concerns are all resolved by Paradox? How would people feel about playing a Vampire game where the whole Caine thing is actually part of the tale of the Triat? Or Werewlf players about finding out that the Triat was actually a misunderstood tidbit from the Caine mythology? Many Mage players complain that they feel the Triat is forced on Mage's core mythology like a straight-jacket two sizes too small, so how would they feel when that became canon? Or, vice versa, if everyone else found out that their mythologies were just some kind of Reality Zone under the aegis of Mage's Tellurian? Because those are genuine concerns with a stated goal of ONE World of Darkness. It seems like a &quot;Grand Reconciliation&quot; would be in order, and I'm not sure who is going to be happy with that.... (Except for the partisans of the line that gets &quot;mythological precedence&quot;, which sounds like it's probably going to be Vampire)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I have a shitload of different RPG's on my shelves. Some of them I want for the setting. Others I want for the rules. Yet others I have out of nostalgia and weird acts of research. All of them are there to keep me amused. As I've said at the beginning of the One World of Darkness announcement, this smells of a &quot;Grand Reconciliation&quot;. It's about creating homgenousness for the sake of the IP being more solid and crossovers being more viable. I do not care for it. I play the WoD games for the clever ideas and cool setting elements, most of which only work as long as you can take the games as not being a part of the single whole.<br /> <br /> What this means is that I will have shelves of editions of White Wolf games that I actually want to play and more money for other RPG's, rather then a kumbayah yogurt that will sacrifice fidelity and tone for the sake of everyone being one big happy family.<br /> <br /> Oh and Ajax, this is the first time iIve heard of the idea that Two color Werewolf and Captain Planet Werewolf are bandied around as anything but insults and putdowns. If it's something people amuse themselves with, good for them, but I've never seen that, I mean just look at this thread. It's all about discrediting Werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T20:11:21-08:00","id":843766,"title":"","content":"I was kind of joking about Teenwolf and Twilight being the same as W:tA werewolves. Though I think that the similarity exists for a reason. Hereditary controlled shape shifting works well when you want a community of werewolf protagonists in who have their own culture, politics, ideology, and so on. That is the main selling point for all WoD games, that show natural creatures aren't just a set of powers or weaknesses, but they are a culture as well.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can do that if all you have are Laun Chaney said werewolves and o got randomly infected and have to shape change during the full moon and only during the full moon. That may make for an interesting movie or maybe even a single character in an RPG, but not an entire role playing games group and especially not a society of supernatural creatures. That is why hereditary voluntary shape changers works for W:tA and for some other works of fiction too.<br /> <br /> So, I don't know if I understand the criticism of W:tA that says that it can't replicate werewolf myths. Modern pop-culture werewolves (Old Hollywood horror) don't fit into RPG's much less the cultures that WW creates. Go back before the modern era and werewolf myths are so varied (and in most cases obscure) that trying to emulate them seems a bit pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T23:15:26-08:00","id":843828,"title":"","content":"While I have some biases.I started with Werewolf the Apocalypse 2e in '94 and part of the appeal was that it WASN'T like pop culture werewolves. Obviously I can't speak for others but for me that was part of the appeal, not a distraction. On the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; thing. Personally I liked the idea of crossover. While I wonder how they will work out the cosmologies I never liked the whole separate Worlds of Darkness set up and look forward to what they do from a mechanical angle to make crossover work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T00:48:26-08:00","id":843852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843354#post843354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today the most famous werewolves aren't the garous, or Jacob Black from Twightlight books, but the main characters from teleserie &quot;Teen Wolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you don't go to a lot of very Werewolf specific sites, blogs, or forums then. Avoid Tumblr blogs where Teen Wolf has a huge fandom of it's very own or places where Twilight fans hang out. Period. Try seeking places that like to play the 2004 Van Helsing Werewolf transformation gif. on infinite loop for example...<br /> Sure you might get some W:tA or W:tF sites that like to use that gif. sometimes, but the people into Werewolves that have very impossible set standards for them use that gif. a lot.<br /> Yes, I've seen some of those type of werewolf fans dislike Teen Wolf as well.<br /> <br /> Another clue is if you can find places that like to post Goldenwolf's Furry vs. Werewolf image. The one that states the major differences between a Furry and a Werewolf.<br /> And even Goldenwolf's art can be derided as being too &quot;Hippie Wolf&quot; among some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My opinion is WoD videogames would need a new setting because storytelling system isn't easy to be adapted. </div> </div> </div>If it is so hard to adapt, then please explain why Vampire: Bloodlines has such a huge following even now. Even among video gamers who aren't aware of the RPG books.<br /> I would like to hear your reasoning as to why since it's still being played with and can be bought on Steam.<br /> Or why the Hunter: the Reckoning console games gained their own cult following.<br /> <br /> I think Linkara of Atop the Fourth Wall had a great point with the massive background setting some comic books have and how they aren't a true deterrent for some people getting into the material. Yes, you can have all this massive backstory going on with some other main story being the main focus. But it still makes people/newcomers interested in some of the backstory and they want to find out more or learn more.<br /> The Rage CCG was my gateway into W:tA. And I'm sure it was for many others. And others have gotten in from other side sources.<br /> So Paradox making the video games might make more people to look into the Tabletop books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T01:00:29-08:00","id":843853,"title":"","content":"I don't see why a system that - even if I disagree with the assumption - is difficult to use in a modern videogame would also entail changing the setting.<br /> <br /> The oWoD is not the Storyteller system and vice versa. If you were a masochist, you could run the oWoD in GURPS (there was even an official version of just that!) or in 3.5 DnD, or (less masochistically <i>by far</i>) FATE. Difficulties porting the system have more or less no bearing in using the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T01:23:02-08:00","id":843856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843828#post843828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I have some biases.I started with Werewolf the Apocalypse 2e in '94 and part of the appeal was that it WASN'T like pop culture werewolves. Obviously I can't speak for others but for me that was part of the appeal, not a distraction. On the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; thing. Personally I liked the idea of crossover. While I wonder how they will work out the cosmologies I never liked the whole separate Worlds of Darkness set up and look forward to what they do from a mechanical angle to make crossover work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanical part never was the biggest problem. The problem is that if you scratch below the surface some of the games completley invalidate the settings and core precepts of other games by their existance - Werewolf and Mage, I'm looking at you :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843853#post843853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why a system that - even if I disagree with the assumption - is difficult to use in a modern videogame would also entail changing the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but that's the point. We are getting setting changes, whether we will like them or not :P. Take a look at what BNS did with Werewolf with White Wolf's blessing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T02:04:32-08:00","id":843862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843856#post843856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mechanical part never was the biggest problem. The problem is that if you scratch below the surface some of the games completley invalidate the settings and core precepts of other games by their existance - Werewolf and Mage, I'm looking at you :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, but that's the point. We are getting setting changes, whether we will like them or not :P. Take a look at what BNS did with Werewolf with White Wolf's blessing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was the biggest problem. I mentioned it because I am curious how the mechanics will change to accommodate crossover.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T02:28:29-08:00","id":843864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843862#post843862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say it was the biggest problem. I mentioned it because I am curious how the mechanics will change to accommodate crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't right now? Outside a couple of weird ideas about special stats that only exist in one game and that stupidity that tied power levels to total dots without considering what 5 means in some games, the system survives most crossovers pretty well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T13:50:22-08:00","id":844132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843647#post843647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh and Ajax, this is the first time iIve heard of the idea that Two color Werewolf and Captain Planet Werewolf are bandied around as anything but insults and putdowns. If it's something people amuse themselves with, good for them, but I've never seen that, I mean just look at this thread. It's all about discrediting Werewolf.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not and cannot fundamentally disagree with you on the way the terms are used. Disparagement is the intent. However, shoveling that steaming pile of manure aside, what is meant as a criticism is ultimately defanged (whoops, sorry about that one) when it is parsed. WtA and Captain Planet definitely share some fundamental themes and those themes are just as good as many/any others if that's the game people want to play. For WtA, being huge furry killing machines with nature on their side fighting the evils of pollution and corruption with claws and magic set against the background of a (probably) fruitless struggle in a (possibly) doomed word? Why not? I once worked for a state highway department doing survey work (archaeological) well in advance of highway construction. There were MANY times we would come out of a multi-mile sweaty hike through the woods carrying way too much HEAVY gear into some of the most breathtakingly beautiful and pristine areas I've seen. Check the map and see the center line of the new road would obliterate the place. I can get behind a game that allows people to feel some visceral virtual relief from that kind of crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:13:52-08:00","id":844143,"title":"","content":"The wonderful old B&amp;W Werewolf movie as is wouldn't make a good game. Probably because it ends so soon and so tragically. Who knows if there wasn't some degree of control he could have achieved? After all it isn't the story of a group of people, it's one guy. If a small group had all been bitten, it might have been a completely different story. Especially if they had been willing to go back to the gypsy and get some solid info.<br /> <br /> But having a group of people being bitten and infected can't leave to a game where multiple individuals are separately infected and still become a group. Ahem.... (Points over at Vampire).<br /> <br /> Sure, werewolf myths are varied. But so are vampire myths. In fact, the Clans in Vampire are a grab bag of many of those myths, legends and modern interpretations thereof (up to and including the whole &quot;Caine&quot; thing...).<br /> <br /> Werewolf Tribes aren't. They are a few random cultural elements worn as pretty thin mufti for some groups, some other culture-types that are just outright shoehorning something that wasn't even vaguely related werewolves or shapeshifters into a Tribe plus a few that exist as an artifact of the rules. There DEFINITELY could be werewolf tribes (and other Fera) based more closely on some version of older stories and more modern takes on the same ideas. And, no, for what values of werewolf legends, myths and fiction were connected to animism and totemism, it was a far cry from the mirror-hopping bastardized modern neo-pagan shamanism-light that is the core mythology and magic of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> And, sure, that could be something that creates an appeal in its own right, but it's kind of having a game where vampires are an obligate cannibalistic sub-species of human that has been living side-by-side with humanity since the Upper Paleolithic who are separated into groups based on their favorite part of the human body they preferentially munch on and the enhancements they gain from said noshing. Oh, and somehow one group or subset of the species as a whole has some inherent control (or at least greater control) of something resembling magic. Though you don't get the whole Rice-ian &quot;sexy vamps&quot; who cause orgasms as they sip, but there's definitely tons of legends and stories around the world that could be plundered for material. Oh, and make them like cuckoos or something. They insert their spawn like (real) changelings into normal human families and realize their vampire selves later on in what usually ends up being a yummy binge on the folks that raised you. As opposed to those raised by vamp parents. (See? Already dividing them up...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:13:18-08:00","id":844306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=843864#post843864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't right now? Outside a couple of weird ideas about special stats that only exist in one game and that stupidity that tied power levels to total dots without considering what 5 means in some games, the system survives most crossovers pretty well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Both because I detest when people trying to springboard off a post of mine with something I didn't say and because the many issues of crossover mechanics is well chronicled in WoD's history. I'll let just leave you to think whatever it is you are going to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:11:32-08:00","id":844370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/830298-interview-with-new-white-wolf?p=844306#post844306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both because I detest when people trying to springboard off a post of mine with something I didn't say and because the many issues of crossover mechanics is well chronicled in WoD's history. I'll let just leave you to think whatever it is you are going to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just... that I find the settings a bigger problem to the crossover then I do the rules. After playing practically all of the WoD for 20 years I am quite well aware of the systems limitations and it's not that much work to get it working. I haven't played it like that in the better part of the last 10 years mostly because I do not want to dilute the games I'm running, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}